window.SIYAHI_DATA = {"poems":[{"number":1,"id":"poem-1","title":"नया है कुछ, अच्छा है","subtitle":"Naya Hai Kuch, Achha Hai","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Joy in newness — a new companion, a new chapter. The same journey, a new traveller. The same life, but a fresh page.","searchText":"Poem 01 नया है कुछ, अच्छा है Naya Hai Kuch, Achha Hai वक्त से अनुमान लगाओ, तो अभी भी थोड़ा कच्चा है... सफर वही है बस, राही नया है... खुमार सा है कुछ, अच्छा है ...! नजरों से अनुमान हो, तो अंजान सा ही रिश्ता है... मुस्कान वोही है बस, वजह नयी है... जज़्बात से है कुछ, अच्छा है ...! बातों से परखना चाहो, तो दोस्त काफी सच्चा है... लॉरेल वोही है बस, हार्डी नया है, नजराना सा है कुछ, अच्छा है ...! फासलो से निखारना हो, तो काफी कुछ बयान है... सफर बड़ा है, और आदत बन गया है... शिकायत नहीं है कुछ, अच्छा है...! सियाही लेके निकला हूं... राह पर कागज मिला है... जिंदगी वही है बस... ये पन्ना नया है... पलटना बिलकुल नहीं इसे, अच्छा है ...! — ssp Joy in newness — a new companion, a new chapter. The same journey, a new traveller. The same life, but a fresh page.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        वक्त से अनुमान लगाओ,<br/>\n        तो अभी भी थोड़ा कच्चा है...<br/>\n        सफर वही है बस, राही नया है...<br/>\n        खुमार सा है कुछ, अच्छा है ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        नजरों से अनुमान हो,<br/>\n        तो अंजान सा ही रिश्ता है...<br/>\n        मुस्कान वोही है बस, वजह नयी है...<br/>\n        जज़्बात से है कुछ, अच्छा है ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        बातों से परखना चाहो,<br/>\n        तो दोस्त काफी सच्चा है...<br/>\n        लॉरेल वोही है बस, हार्डी नया है,<br/>\n        नजराना सा है कुछ, अच्छा है ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        फासलो से निखारना हो,<br/>\n        तो काफी कुछ बयान है...<br/>\n        सफर बड़ा है, और आदत बन गया है...<br/>\n        शिकायत नहीं है कुछ, अच्छा है...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        सियाही लेके निकला हूं...<br/>\n        राह पर कागज मिला है...<br/>\n        जिंदगी वही है बस... ये पन्ना नया है...<br/>\n        पलटना बिलकुल नहीं इसे, अच्छा है ...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Joy in newness — a new companion, a new chapter. The same journey, a new traveller. The same life, but a fresh page.</div>\n","featuredRank":10},{"number":2,"id":"poem-2","title":"Sitara","subtitle":"The Star","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A star appeared in darkness and filled life with joy, like love found unexpectedly. The flower stopped blooming, went unnoticed — but the memory of that encounter became a deep, intoxicating love.","searchText":"Poem 02 Sitara The Star Darawna sa andhera thha, kahinse jab ek sitara khil gya... Cheez mamuli nhi bhai, sarein khushiyonka pitara thha mil gya... Guldasta khubsoorat par usne najane, mehekna kyu chhod diya... Khushbu ki talash mein koi usey, khareedna hi bhul gya..... Adhura thha, anjan thha, par wakif tabse ishq se bann gya... Yaad karke sare pal eksath, gehre nashe sa chadh gya... Yaad hai unse pehli hi mulakat se bs, sama sa thha bann gya... Khoj khwaishonki thhi, aur khuda hi mil gya... — ssp A star appeared in darkness and filled life with joy, like love found unexpectedly. The flower stopped blooming, went unnoticed — but the memory of that encounter became a deep, intoxicating love.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Darawna sa andhera thha,<br/>\n        kahinse jab ek sitara khil gya...<br/>\n        Cheez mamuli nhi bhai,<br/>\n        sarein khushiyonka pitara thha mil gya...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Guldasta khubsoorat par usne najane, mehekna kyu chhod diya...<br/>\n        Khushbu ki talash mein koi usey, khareedna hi bhul gya.....\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Adhura thha, anjan thha, par wakif tabse ishq se bann gya...<br/>\n        Yaad karke sare pal eksath, gehre nashe sa chadh gya...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Yaad hai unse pehli hi mulakat se bs, sama sa thha bann gya...<br/>\n        Khoj khwaishonki thhi, aur khuda hi mil gya...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A star appeared in darkness and filled life with joy, like love found unexpectedly. The flower stopped blooming, went unnoticed — but the memory of that encounter became a deep, intoxicating love.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":3,"id":"poem-3","title":"Intezaar","subtitle":"Waiting","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A longing for the beloved's voice and her warmth — even her complaints. A simple prayer: may you find every happiness, because one smile from you lights up the entire world.","searchText":"Poem 03 Intezaar Waiting Intzar rehta hai... Aapki saasonka... jab hmara naam leti ho... Shikayat bhari batonka... jab dil se do jam leti ho... Khuda krein aapko milein sari khushiya jo maujud ho iss duniya mein... Kyunki ek lazmi muskurahat se Sare jaha ko bhi khush kar deti ho... — ssp A longing for the beloved's voice and her warmth — even her complaints. A simple prayer: may you find every happiness, because one smile from you lights up the entire world.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Intzar rehta hai...<br/>\n        Aapki saasonka... jab hmara naam leti ho...<br/>\n        Shikayat bhari batonka... jab dil se do jam leti ho...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Khuda krein aapko milein sari khushiya jo maujud ho iss duniya mein...<br/>\n        Kyunki ek lazmi muskurahat se Sare jaha ko bhi khush kar deti ho...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A longing for the beloved's voice and her warmth — even her complaints. A simple prayer: may you find every happiness, because one smile from you lights up the entire world.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":4,"id":"poem-4","title":"Wo Khoobsurat","subtitle":"That Beautiful One","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"An overflowing tribute to someone deeply loved — her beauty, her understanding, her eyes and laughter feel like life itself. The poet admits: no words are ever enough for her.","searchText":"Poem 04 Wo Khoobsurat That Beautiful One Jitni wo khoobsurat hai... sachmein yakeen nhi hota... Uske bina zindagi jeena mtlab jaise, khane mein namak hi nhi hota... Jitna achhese wo hume smjhti hai... utna hum bhi usey jaante hai... Wo humsafar maanti hai shayad, par hum to ab khuda hi maante hai... Ehem hai wo, sabki laadli hai, apne masle sab usey btate hai... Bholi hai aur shatir bhi thodi, jisey hum din raat kaafi satate hai... Itni achhi muskan to meine kisiki nhi dekhi... Sirf mujhe dikhti hai kya jo duniya se pare laagti h... Ankhein bhi ma sha allah sabkuch bayan kar deti hai... Ishq jahir na karna chaho tobhi mehkash sama bandh deti hai... Zulfein to bas, ek alag mayajal hai... itnasa wakht hua jaan ke aur dekho ye haal hai... Ankh band karke baatein hoti hai hmari, mohabbt kaafi bemisaal hai... Meri jaan aur mera jahan hai... har tamanna har armaan hai... Labonpe hmare bas usika naam hai, ishq ki ye gawahi deta hu, Aur bhi jyada pyar hone ka anuman hai... Kya kahu yar smjh nhi ata, jitna bolta hu usse dil bhar nhi pata... Aap sachmein mein wo khushbu hai jo sanson mein bastein hai, Aapke bina ek pal bhi jeeya nhi jata! — ssp An overflowing tribute to someone deeply loved — her beauty, her understanding, her eyes and laughter feel like life itself. The poet admits: no words are ever enough for her.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Jitni wo khoobsurat hai... sachmein yakeen nhi hota...<br/>\n        Uske bina zindagi jeena mtlab jaise, khane mein namak hi nhi hota...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Jitna achhese wo hume smjhti hai... utna hum bhi usey jaante hai...<br/>\n        Wo humsafar maanti hai shayad, par hum to ab khuda hi maante hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ehem hai wo, sabki laadli hai, apne masle sab usey btate hai...<br/>\n        Bholi hai aur shatir bhi thodi, jisey hum din raat kaafi satate hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Itni achhi muskan to meine kisiki nhi dekhi...<br/>\n        Sirf mujhe dikhti hai kya jo duniya se pare laagti h...<br/>\n        Ankhein bhi ma sha allah sabkuch bayan kar deti hai...<br/>\n        Ishq jahir na karna chaho tobhi mehkash sama bandh deti hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Zulfein to bas, ek alag mayajal hai... itnasa wakht hua jaan ke aur dekho ye haal hai...<br/>\n        Ankh band karke baatein hoti hai hmari, mohabbt kaafi bemisaal hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Meri jaan aur mera jahan hai... har tamanna har armaan hai...<br/>\n        Labonpe hmare bas usika naam hai, ishq ki ye gawahi deta hu,<br/>\n        Aur bhi jyada pyar hone ka anuman hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kya kahu yar smjh nhi ata, jitna bolta hu usse dil bhar nhi pata...<br/>\n        Aap sachmein mein wo khushbu hai jo sanson mein bastein hai,<br/>\n        Aapke bina ek pal bhi jeeya nhi jata!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">An overflowing tribute to someone deeply loved — her beauty, her understanding, her eyes and laughter feel like life itself. The poet admits: no words are ever enough for her.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":5,"id":"poem-5","title":"Baadal","subtitle":"The Sky & The Earth","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Clouds don't measure height, and the earth doesn't measure depth. When love has truly dissolved inside the heart, no flaw or bitterness can find entry.","searchText":"Poem 05 Baadal The Sky & The Earth Baadal unchai gina nhi krte... Zameen gehrai napa nhi karti... Jab dilmein hi mohbbat ghul gyi ho, Tab koi burai kbhi dakhal, diya nhi karti... — ssp Clouds don't measure height, and the earth doesn't measure depth. When love has truly dissolved inside the heart, no flaw or bitterness can find entry.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Baadal unchai gina nhi krte...<br/>\n        Zameen gehrai napa nhi karti...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Jab dilmein hi mohbbat ghul gyi ho,<br/>\n        Tab koi burai kbhi dakhal, diya nhi karti...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Clouds don't measure height, and the earth doesn't measure depth. When love has truly dissolved inside the heart, no flaw or bitterness can find entry.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":6,"id":"poem-6","title":"Parchhayi","subtitle":"Shadow","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A shadow walks beside you; loneliness brings rain; love is a form of prayer. The beloved is the shadow, the depth, and life itself — compressed into four quiet lines.","searchText":"Poem 06 Parchhayi Shadow Parchhayi sath deti hai... aur gehraai darr ki ahat... Tanhaai barsaat deti hai... aur pyar uski ibadat... Parchhayi tum ho aur gehrai shiddat hai... Tanhai judaai hai... aur pyar zindagi! — ssp A shadow walks beside you; loneliness brings rain; love is a form of prayer. The beloved is the shadow, the depth, and life itself — compressed into four quiet lines.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Parchhayi sath deti hai... aur gehraai darr ki ahat...<br/>\n        Tanhaai barsaat deti hai... aur pyar uski ibadat...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Parchhayi tum ho aur gehrai shiddat hai...<br/>\n        Tanhai judaai hai... aur pyar zindagi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A shadow walks beside you; loneliness brings rain; love is a form of prayer. The beloved is the shadow, the depth, and life itself — compressed into four quiet lines.</div>\n","featuredRank":1},{"number":7,"id":"poem-7","title":"Un Se","subtitle":"With Them","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Despite distance and misunderstanding, love holds firm. The poet asks for patience, promising that the warmth between them will find its way back.","searchText":"Poem 07 Un Se With Them Unse baat to hoti h, par waisi nhi jaisi hum chahte hai... Mulakaat to hoti h, par waisi nhi jaisi hum mangte hai... Kehti hai wo ajkal, hum bdi sakti se pesh aate hai... Dukh h ji hume bhi, par halaat waise batlaate hai.. Muaf kardo kuch din nacheez ko, shiddat se darkhwast hai... Phir se lautenge jrur wo pyar k kuch pal, Tabtak, ye sare jakhm, mohbbt k liye bardasht hai... — ssp Despite distance and misunderstanding, love holds firm. The poet asks for patience, promising that the warmth between them will find its way back.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Unse baat to hoti h, par waisi nhi jaisi hum chahte hai...<br/>\n        Mulakaat to hoti h, par waisi nhi jaisi hum mangte hai...<br/>\n        Kehti hai wo ajkal, hum bdi sakti se pesh aate hai...<br/>\n        Dukh h ji hume bhi, par halaat waise batlaate hai..\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Muaf kardo kuch din nacheez ko, shiddat se darkhwast hai...<br/>\n        Phir se lautenge jrur wo pyar k kuch pal,<br/>\n        Tabtak, ye sare jakhm, mohbbt k liye bardasht hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Despite distance and misunderstanding, love holds firm. The poet asks for patience, promising that the warmth between them will find its way back.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":8,"id":"poem-8","title":"Kaabu Mein Dil","subtitle":"The Heart Uncontrolled","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Real love cannot be controlled — a God who stays locked in a mosque is no real God. The journey is only life when the beloved meets you on the road.","searchText":"Poem 08 Kaabu Mein Dil The Heart Uncontrolled Kaabu mein dil rahein to wo mohbbt hi kya... Masjid mein bnd rahe wo khudah hi kya... Safar hi manzil na ho wo zindagi hi kya... Raaste mein aap na mile wo qabooool hi kya.... — ssp Real love cannot be controlled — a God who stays locked in a mosque is no real God. The journey is only life when the beloved meets you on the road.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kaabu mein dil rahein to wo mohbbt hi kya...<br/>\n        Masjid mein bnd rahe wo khudah hi kya...<br/>\n        Safar hi manzil na ho wo zindagi hi kya...<br/>\n        Raaste mein aap na mile wo qabooool hi kya....\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Real love cannot be controlled — a God who stays locked in a mosque is no real God. The journey is only life when the beloved meets you on the road.</div>\n","featuredRank":11},{"number":9,"id":"poem-9","title":"सवाल-ए-इश्क","subtitle":"Sawal-e-Ishq","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Why does love consume every soul? Because whether it's fate or luck, everything leads back to the beloved. Love and devotion are one — accepted by God.","searchText":"Poem 09 सवाल-ए-इश्क Sawal-e-Ishq सवाल ये पूछा गया था की, हर जान इश्क में क्यू फनाह है ... जवाब मुराद हो या मुकद्दर, आप ही से जुड़ा है... इश्क केह लो या इबादत, मंजूर-ए-खुदा है ...! — ssp Why does love consume every soul? Because whether it's fate or luck, everything leads back to the beloved. Love and devotion are one — accepted by God.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        सवाल ये पूछा गया था की, हर जान इश्क में क्यू फनाह है ...<br/>\n        जवाब मुराद हो या मुकद्दर, आप ही से जुड़ा है...<br/>\n        इश्क केह लो या इबादत, मंजूर-ए-खुदा है ...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Why does love consume every soul? Because whether it's fate or luck, everything leads back to the beloved. Love and devotion are one — accepted by God.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":10,"id":"poem-10","title":"Ldki Mili","subtitle":"When She Came Along","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Meeting someone doesn't mean you'll ask. Friendship doesn't mean you'll remember. Love doesn't mean fearlessness. And fear doesn't mean silence. Life never follows simple rules.","searchText":"Poem 10 Ldki Mili When She Came Along Ldki mili aur puchh liya aisa nhi hota... Dost mila aur bhul gye aisa nhi hota... Pyar kiya aur darein nhi aisa nhi hota... Darr laga to izhar hi na kiya aisa bhi nhi hota... — ssp Meeting someone doesn't mean you'll ask. Friendship doesn't mean you'll remember. Love doesn't mean fearlessness. And fear doesn't mean silence. Life never follows simple rules.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ldki mili aur puchh liya aisa nhi hota...<br/>\n        Dost mila aur bhul gye aisa nhi hota...<br/>\n        Pyar kiya aur darein nhi aisa nhi hota...<br/>\n        Darr laga to izhar hi na kiya aisa bhi nhi hota...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Meeting someone doesn't mean you'll ask. Friendship doesn't mean you'll remember. Love doesn't mean fearlessness. And fear doesn't mean silence. Life never follows simple rules.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":11,"id":"poem-11","title":"Agar Rakh Sako","subtitle":"If You Could","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A tender plea — take care of yourself, see how much I love you, stay a little longer, and with your eyes, write your name on my heart.","searchText":"Poem 11 Agar Rakh Sako If You Could Agar rakh sako to khudka khayal rakho.. Agar dekh sako to hmara aapke liye pyar dekho... Agar ruk sako to hmare liye thodi der aur ruko... Apne ankhonse hmare dil pe apna naam likho... — ssp A tender plea — take care of yourself, see how much I love you, stay a little longer, and with your eyes, write your name on my heart.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Agar rakh sako to khudka khayal rakho..<br/>\n        Agar dekh sako to hmara aapke liye pyar dekho...<br/>\n        Agar ruk sako to hmare liye thodi der aur ruko...<br/>\n        Apne ankhonse hmare dil pe apna naam likho...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A tender plea — take care of yourself, see how much I love you, stay a little longer, and with your eyes, write your name on my heart.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":12,"id":"poem-12","title":"Nind Mein","subtitle":"In Sleep","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A gentle goodbye to a beloved — lose yourself in dreams, be happy wherever you go, but don't forget to come back.","searchText":"Poem 12 Nind Mein In Sleep Nind mein ghul jao... Sapne dekhna mat bhulna... Jaha bhi jao khush raho yar... Bs palatna mat bhulna! — ssp A gentle goodbye to a beloved — lose yourself in dreams, be happy wherever you go, but don't forget to come back.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Nind mein ghul jao...<br/>\n        Sapne dekhna mat bhulna...<br/>\n        Jaha bhi jao khush raho yar...<br/>\n        Bs palatna mat bhulna!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A gentle goodbye to a beloved — lose yourself in dreams, be happy wherever you go, but don't forget to come back.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":13,"id":"poem-13","title":"Bolna Chahta Hu","subtitle":"I Want to Say","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A whole day full of thoughts and people — yet only one person's memory refuses to leave the heart.","searchText":"Poem 13 Bolna Chahta Hu I Want to Say Bolna chahta hu bol nhi pata... Milna chahta hu mil nhi pata... Kitne khyal ate hai dinbhar, Kitne log milte hai dinbhar, Par bs ek aapka khyal hai jo dilse nhi jata... — ssp A whole day full of thoughts and people — yet only one person's memory refuses to leave the heart.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Bolna chahta hu bol nhi pata...<br/>\n        Milna chahta hu mil nhi pata...<br/>\n        Kitne khyal ate hai dinbhar,<br/>\n        Kitne log milte hai dinbhar,<br/>\n        Par bs ek aapka khyal hai jo dilse nhi jata...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A whole day full of thoughts and people — yet only one person's memory refuses to leave the heart.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":14,"id":"poem-14","title":"Wakht Khuddar","subtitle":"Time Grows Proud","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Time has grown proud, widening the gap between seeing and meeting. Love cannot be felt at this close distance anymore — a quiet realization of growing apart.","searchText":"Poem 14 Wakht Khuddar Time Grows Proud Wakht khuddar hone lga hai... Dikhne aur milne ke bich antar samajhne lga hai... Iradein aur hakikat mein ek lakeer si bann gyi hai.. Pyarr ka ehsas pass rehkar nhi hota, ye abhi suljhne lga hai... — ssp Time has grown proud, widening the gap between seeing and meeting. Love cannot be felt at this close distance anymore — a quiet realization of growing apart.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wakht khuddar hone lga hai...<br/>\n        Dikhne aur milne ke bich antar samajhne lga hai...<br/>\n        Iradein aur hakikat mein ek lakeer si bann gyi hai..<br/>\n        Pyarr ka ehsas pass rehkar nhi hota, ye abhi suljhne lga hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Time has grown proud, widening the gap between seeing and meeting. Love cannot be felt at this close distance anymore — a quiet realization of growing apart.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":15,"id":"poem-15","title":"Dua","subtitle":"A Prayer","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A prayer for the beloved's happiness — may she always smile, never know sorrow, and always have beside her the one who makes her life bloom.","searchText":"Poem 15 Dua A Prayer Har lamha apke hothon pe ek muskan rahe, Har gum se aap hmesha anjaan rahen, Jiske sath mehek uthti hai aapki zindgi, Hamsha aapke pass bs wohi ek insan rahe! Dua to usey diyi jaati hai jise uski jrurat ho... Aap par markar roj krenge pyaar agar aapki ijajat ho! — ssp A prayer for the beloved's happiness — may she always smile, never know sorrow, and always have beside her the one who makes her life bloom.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Har lamha apke hothon pe ek muskan rahe,<br/>\n        Har gum se aap hmesha anjaan rahen,<br/>\n        Jiske sath mehek uthti hai aapki zindgi,<br/>\n        Hamsha aapke pass bs wohi ek insan rahe!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dua to usey diyi jaati hai jise uski jrurat ho...<br/>\n        Aap par markar roj krenge pyaar agar aapki ijajat ho!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A prayer for the beloved's happiness — may she always smile, never know sorrow, and always have beside her the one who makes her life bloom.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":16,"id":"poem-16","title":"Man Behle","subtitle":"When the Heart Wanders","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Come when the heart wanders, smile when it races, appear when the eyes close — and in the next life, simply be mine.","searchText":"Poem 16 Man Behle When the Heart Wanders Man behle to pass ajana... Dil dhadke to thoda muskurana... Palak jhapke to chehra samne lana... Agle jnam mein hi sahi par, hmare ho jana. — ssp Come when the heart wanders, smile when it races, appear when the eyes close — and in the next life, simply be mine.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Man behle to pass ajana...<br/>\n        Dil dhadke to thoda muskurana...<br/>\n        Palak jhapke to chehra samne lana...<br/>\n        Agle jnam mein hi sahi par, hmare ho jana.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Come when the heart wanders, smile when it races, appear when the eyes close — and in the next life, simply be mine.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":17,"id":"poem-17","title":"ज़िन्दगी की खुशियां","subtitle":"Zindagi Ki Khushiyan","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"All my joys exist because of you — half from teasing you, and the other half from making up with you.","searchText":"Poem 17 ज़िन्दगी की खुशियां Zindagi Ki Khushiyan ज़िन्दगी की मेरी सारी खुशियां तो तेरे बहाने से है ... आधी तुझे सताने से है, और बाकी मनाने से है ...! — ssp All my joys exist because of you — half from teasing you, and the other half from making up with you.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        ज़िन्दगी की मेरी सारी खुशियां तो तेरे बहाने से है ...<br/>\n        आधी तुझे सताने से है, और बाकी मनाने से है ...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">All my joys exist because of you — half from teasing you, and the other half from making up with you.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":18,"id":"poem-18","title":"Kasoor","subtitle":"The Fault","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Neither was at fault — one played the friend, the other hid the love. She slept on his chest, completely unaware; he even stilled his own heartbeat so her sleep would not break.","searchText":"Poem 18 Kasoor The Fault Kasoor na unka thha na mera... hum dono hi rishton ki rasmein nibhate rahe... Wo dosti ka ehsas jatate rahe... aur hum mohbbt ko dil mein chhupate rahe! Wo mere dil par sar rakhkar soyi hui thhi bekhbar... Humne to dhadkan hi rok diyi ki kahi uski nind na tut jayein! Wo kareeb to bohot hai, mgar dooriyon ke sath... Hum jee to rahe hai, mgar majburiyonke sath... — ssp Neither was at fault — one played the friend, the other hid the love. She slept on his chest, completely unaware; he even stilled his own heartbeat so her sleep would not break.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kasoor na unka thha na mera... hum dono hi rishton ki rasmein nibhate rahe...<br/>\n        Wo dosti ka ehsas jatate rahe... aur hum mohbbt ko dil mein chhupate rahe!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wo mere dil par sar rakhkar soyi hui thhi bekhbar...<br/>\n        Humne to dhadkan hi rok diyi ki kahi uski nind na tut jayein!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wo kareeb to bohot hai, mgar dooriyon ke sath...<br/>\n        Hum jee to rahe hai, mgar majburiyonke sath...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Neither was at fault — one played the friend, the other hid the love. She slept on his chest, completely unaware; he even stilled his own heartbeat so her sleep would not break.</div>\n","featuredRank":2},{"number":19,"id":"poem-19","title":"Raatonka Agaaz","subtitle":"The Beginning of Nights","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Nights begin with great energy and heat, but they always, without fail, end in pain.","searchText":"Poem 19 Raatonka Agaaz The Beginning of Nights Raatonka agaaz to bahut joshila hota hai... Par anjaam hmesha dard de jata hai... — ssp Nights begin with great energy and heat, but they always, without fail, end in pain.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Raatonka agaaz to bahut joshila hota hai...<br/>\n        Par anjaam hmesha dard de jata hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Nights begin with great energy and heat, but they always, without fail, end in pain.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":20,"id":"poem-20","title":"Ek Pal","subtitle":"That One Afternoon","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Not a single moment passes without remembering that afternoon — when she was so beautiful he couldn't look away, and she pretended to sulk just so he'd sing her back.","searchText":"Poem 20 Ek Pal That One Afternoon Ek pal bhi aisa nhi Jab wo lamhe yaad na ayein... Ek dopher thhi jisme laga, Bichmein koi aur na ayein... Itni khubsurat lag rahi thhi aap ki bs ab raha na jayein... Jante hai, aap ruthhi thhi thodi der, Taaki hum gaa kar aapko manayein! — ssp Not a single moment passes without remembering that afternoon — when she was so beautiful he couldn't look away, and she pretended to sulk just so he'd sing her back.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ek pal bhi aisa nhi<br/>\n        Jab wo lamhe yaad na ayein...<br/>\n        Ek dopher thhi jisme laga,<br/>\n        Bichmein koi aur na ayein...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Itni khubsurat lag rahi thhi aap ki bs ab raha na jayein...<br/>\n        Jante hai, aap ruthhi thhi thodi der,<br/>\n        Taaki hum gaa kar aapko manayein!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Not a single moment passes without remembering that afternoon — when she was so beautiful he couldn't look away, and she pretended to sulk just so he'd sing her back.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":21,"id":"poem-21","title":"Moonlight","subtitle":"Stuck in the Moonlight","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Stuck in moonlight with you was one of the things done right. Memories fade, people change you — so choose your company carefully. Life is not a simple game.","searchText":"Poem 21 Moonlight Stuck in the Moonlight Stuck in the moonlight wid u.... One of the things done right wid u... Memories are too many.... some fade away! Fake won't stay long.... but right one finds the way! People can change us... personality is like a clay! So be careful with your choices, life is not an easy game to play! — ssp Stuck in moonlight with you was one of the things done right. Memories fade, people change you — so choose your company carefully. Life is not a simple game.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Stuck in the moonlight wid u....<br/>\n        One of the things done right wid u...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Memories are too many.... some fade away!<br/>\n        Fake won't stay long.... but right one finds the way!<br/>\n        People can change us... personality is like a clay!<br/>\n        So be careful with your choices, life is not an easy game to play!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Stuck in moonlight with you was one of the things done right. Memories fade, people change you — so choose your company carefully. Life is not a simple game.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":22,"id":"poem-22","title":"इतनी भी","subtitle":"Itni Bhi","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Don't get so used to just listening to me that I forget to tell you — and my love ends up staying locked inside, never spoken.","searchText":"Poem 22 इतनी भी Itni Bhi इतनी भी सुनने की आदत मत लगाना, की हम बताना भूल जाएं... और हमारे दिल की मोहब्बत, दिलमें ही रहे जाएं...! — ssp Don't get so used to just listening to me that I forget to tell you — and my love ends up staying locked inside, never spoken.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        इतनी भी सुनने की आदत मत लगाना,<br/>\n        की हम बताना भूल जाएं...<br/>\n        और हमारे दिल की मोहब्बत,<br/>\n        दिलमें ही रहे जाएं...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Don't get so used to just listening to me that I forget to tell you — and my love ends up staying locked inside, never spoken.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":23,"id":"poem-23","title":"एक सपना","subtitle":"Ek Sapna — A Dream","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Once dreamed of loving you; you made it real by letting me try. Today I woke not from a dream, but to reality — the most beautiful surprise of all.","searchText":"Poem 23 एक सपना Ek Sapna — A Dream एक सपना देखा था कभी, आप से प्यार करने का... पूरा किया आपने इजाजत देकर, एक मौका ईजहार करने का... चैन की निंद थी आज, सपना न था पर आज आपका... पहली बार निंद खुली और, हकीकत को मौका मिला सपने से बहार होने का....! — ssp Once dreamed of loving you; you made it real by letting me try. Today I woke not from a dream, but to reality — the most beautiful surprise of all.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        एक सपना देखा था कभी, आप से प्यार करने का...<br/>\n        पूरा किया आपने इजाजत देकर, एक मौका ईजहार करने का...<br/>\n        चैन की निंद थी आज, सपना न था पर आज आपका...<br/>\n        पहली बार निंद खुली और, हकीकत को मौका मिला सपने से बहार होने का....!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Once dreamed of loving you; you made it real by letting me try. Today I woke not from a dream, but to reality — the most beautiful surprise of all.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":24,"id":"poem-24","title":"सोचा उन रातों पे","subtitle":"Socha Un Raaton Pe","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"On nights you don't appear in dreams, I think I'll write poetry — but those nights are unbearable too. Our moments were beautiful, but you were more so; my complaints are real, but not greater than my love.","searchText":"Poem 24 सोचा उन रातों पे Socha Un Raaton Pe सोचा उन रातों पे शेर बनाते हैं, जब आपके सपने नहीं आते... पर उनपर लिखना तो दूर, ऐसी रातें हम झेल ही नहीं पाते... क्योंकि साथ बिताए लम्हें खूबसूरत थे, पर आपसे ज्यादा नही... शिकायत तो जरूर होगी आपको हमसे, मगर...प्यार से ज्यादा नहीं...! — ssp On nights you don't appear in dreams, I think I'll write poetry — but those nights are unbearable too. Our moments were beautiful, but you were more so; my complaints are real, but not greater than my love.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        सोचा उन रातों पे शेर बनाते हैं,<br/>\n        जब आपके सपने नहीं आते...<br/>\n        पर उनपर लिखना तो दूर,<br/>\n        ऐसी रातें हम झेल ही नहीं पाते...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        क्योंकि साथ बिताए लम्हें खूबसूरत थे,<br/>\n        पर आपसे ज्यादा नही...<br/>\n        शिकायत तो जरूर होगी आपको हमसे,<br/>\n        मगर...प्यार से ज्यादा नहीं...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">On nights you don't appear in dreams, I think I'll write poetry — but those nights are unbearable too. Our moments were beautiful, but you were more so; my complaints are real, but not greater than my love.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":25,"id":"poem-25","title":"Kavita Par","subtitle":"Writing a Poem on You","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"When trying to write a poem about you, even words refused. They said: how can we describe the life you've lived? Bloom always — so others find a reason to smile just by seeing you.","searchText":"Poem 25 Kavita Par Writing a Poem on You Sawalo jawabon mein uljhe to kon suljhaega... Iss koyle ko chhu kar to dekho... heera ban jayega... Kavita kar raha thha aap pe... Par lafz hi na mile... Wobhi bole: aapne jiyi zindagi jo, Usey hum kya bayan kare... Phool pata nhi kyu aaj hi na khile... Bole aap aao jab zindagi mein, Tab bata diya kare! Isilie rehna hmesha khilte bs aap... Taaki dusron ko bhi aapko dekhkar, Muskurane ki ek to wjah mile! — ssp When trying to write a poem about you, even words refused. They said: how can we describe the life you've lived? Bloom always — so others find a reason to smile just by seeing you.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sawalo jawabon mein uljhe to kon suljhaega...<br/>\n        Iss koyle ko chhu kar to dekho... heera ban jayega...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kavita kar raha thha aap pe...<br/>\n        Par lafz hi na mile...<br/>\n        Wobhi bole: aapne jiyi zindagi jo,<br/>\n        Usey hum kya bayan kare...<br/>\n        Phool pata nhi kyu aaj hi na khile...<br/>\n        Bole aap aao jab zindagi mein,<br/>\n        Tab bata diya kare!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Isilie rehna hmesha khilte bs aap...<br/>\n        Taaki dusron ko bhi aapko dekhkar,<br/>\n        Muskurane ki ek to wjah mile!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">When trying to write a poem about you, even words refused. They said: how can we describe the life you've lived? Bloom always — so others find a reason to smile just by seeing you.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":26,"id":"poem-26","title":"Khwab Aya","subtitle":"The Dream Came","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Your dream came last night and brought back a lost smile. Every gift, every conversation remembered. Since you rarely come in daylight, a dream became the only reliable way to meet you.","searchText":"Poem 26 Khwab Aya The Dream Came Aj hi aapka khwab aya thha.. Ek khoyi si muskan wapas laya thha... Aap dikhe thhe usmein... Haste khelte muskurate... Garmi ke mausam mein jaise dil behlane wala anokha sawan aya thha... Har baat yaad hai jabse mile hai aapse... haar gift... har topic jo dhundkar laya thha... Pehchan aapki thhi par ehsas hmara thha... Aaj hi ki baat hai... aap ka khwab aya thha... Ab bs aaj ka din kaat jayein ye khwaish thhi mann mein... Kyunki milte to aap ho nhi jyada aajkal dinmein... To aap se milne ka ek bharosemand zariya paya thha... Woi khwab wapas aaye kal bhi jo aaj aya thha... 2 saal pehle zindagi mein ye mehman aya thha... Usi se kiyi thhi mohabbt aur kiya waada nibhaya thha... Pata nhi kaha le jayein ye zindagi hume, par Yaad jrur rahegi wo raat... Jab aap ka ye khwab aya thha... Kavita bann gyi baton baton mein, par sach kahu to... Izhar karne ka humne to ye bs ek bahana paya thha...! — ssp Your dream came last night and brought back a lost smile. Every gift, every conversation remembered. Since you rarely come in daylight, a dream became the only reliable way to meet you.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Aj hi aapka khwab aya thha..<br/>\n        Ek khoyi si muskan wapas laya thha...<br/>\n        Aap dikhe thhe usmein...<br/>\n        Haste khelte muskurate...<br/>\n        Garmi ke mausam mein jaise dil behlane wala anokha sawan aya thha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Har baat yaad hai jabse mile hai aapse... haar gift... har topic jo dhundkar laya thha...<br/>\n        Pehchan aapki thhi par ehsas hmara thha...<br/>\n        Aaj hi ki baat hai... aap ka khwab aya thha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ab bs aaj ka din kaat jayein ye khwaish thhi mann mein...<br/>\n        Kyunki milte to aap ho nhi jyada aajkal dinmein...<br/>\n        To aap se milne ka ek bharosemand zariya paya thha...<br/>\n        Woi khwab wapas aaye kal bhi jo aaj aya thha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        2 saal pehle zindagi mein ye mehman aya thha...<br/>\n        Usi se kiyi thhi mohabbt aur kiya waada nibhaya thha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Pata nhi kaha le jayein ye zindagi hume, par<br/>\n        Yaad jrur rahegi wo raat...<br/>\n        Jab aap ka ye khwab aya thha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kavita bann gyi baton baton mein, par sach kahu to...<br/>\n        Izhar karne ka humne to ye bs ek bahana paya thha...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Your dream came last night and brought back a lost smile. Every gift, every conversation remembered. Since you rarely come in daylight, a dream became the only reliable way to meet you.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":27,"id":"poem-27","title":"लोग पूछते हैं","subtitle":"Log Poochhtey Hain","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"People ask where words come from — search the lane you walk through. People ask how to love — does a bud ask how to bloom? Love is our nature; fate is its request.","searchText":"Poem 27 लोग पूछते हैं Log Poochhtey Hain लोग पूछते हैं, लफ्ज़ आपको, मिलते कहासे हैं ? केहता हूं, ढूंढो उस गलीमें, आप गुजरते जहा से हैं... लोग पूछते हैं, प्यार करना हो, तो करते कैसे हैं? केहता हूं, कली से कोई पूछता है भला, की खिलते कैसे हैं... खिलना उसकी आदत हैं, और खुशबू उसका एहसास... प्यार हमारी फितरत हैं, और किस्मत उसकी दरखास्त... पूछते तो लोग कई सवाल हैं, कई दीवानोके कई बवाल हैं... कैसे सुलझे इससे, किसे बताएं ? खयालों के आंगन में, बस यही सवाल हैं..! — ssp People ask where words come from — search the lane you walk through. People ask how to love — does a bud ask how to bloom? Love is our nature; fate is its request.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        लोग पूछते हैं, लफ्ज़ आपको, मिलते कहासे हैं ?<br/>\n        केहता हूं, ढूंढो उस गलीमें,<br/>\n        आप गुजरते जहा से हैं...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        लोग पूछते हैं, प्यार करना हो, तो करते कैसे हैं?<br/>\n        केहता हूं, कली से कोई पूछता है भला,<br/>\n        की खिलते कैसे हैं...<br/>\n        खिलना उसकी आदत हैं,<br/>\n        और खुशबू उसका एहसास...<br/>\n        प्यार हमारी फितरत हैं,<br/>\n        और किस्मत उसकी दरखास्त...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पूछते तो लोग कई सवाल हैं,<br/>\n        कई दीवानोके कई बवाल हैं...<br/>\n        कैसे सुलझे इससे, किसे बताएं ?<br/>\n        खयालों के आंगन में, बस यही सवाल हैं..!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">People ask where words come from — search the lane you walk through. People ask how to love — does a bud ask how to bloom? Love is our nature; fate is its request.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":28,"id":"poem-28","title":"Puchhna Mat","subtitle":"Don't Ask How I Am","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Don't ask how I am — I won't be able to say. It'll take time. This poem isn't blame — it's just truth. And someday, if we meet again, I'll just smile and hold you close.","searchText":"Poem 28 Puchhna Mat Don't Ask How I Am Context: after separation, when she asks — how are you? Puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge... Thoda wakht lgega shayad, jbtak hum samhal jaenge... Ilzam kitne lage pta nhi, par sajah to ek hi mil gyi... Wakht se jab lagayi shart, tab asli aukat dikh gyi... Manzil nhi jinhe op aise raston pe chal pade thhe... Ab aa gyi to shayad dusra rasta chunn nhi paenge... Puchhna mat hum kaise hai... bta nhi paenge... Harkatein jo lagti thhi wo niyat bann gyi.. Dostike safar mein kyu chahat bann gyi... Kaha thha ishq ho gya hai ab adat na bann jana... Badal nhi paenge... Aapne khair mana nhi... ab smjha nhi paenge... Ab puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge... Khuddar thhe hum shayad jab iska alam kiya... Dildar thhe aap jab sath har dum diya... Kahani aisi bann gyi ki adhuri keh nhi paenge... Zid mat karna kyunki puri suna nhi paenge.. Puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge... Pdhke ye sab aap ab bura na mann lena... Man hi mann kuch yaad krke dil behla lena... Kbhi nhi... aapko gum mein dekh nhi paenge... Kbhi dikhe to kahise aakar hasa de jaenge... Kbhi hue pehle ki tarah to ek hi bar gale mil jaenge... Bs puchhna mat hum kaise hai... bta nhi paenge... — ssp Don't ask how I am — I won't be able to say. It'll take time. This poem isn't blame — it's just truth. And someday, if we meet again, I'll just smile and hold you close.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-note\">Context: after separation, when she asks — how are you?</div>\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Thoda wakht lgega shayad, jbtak hum samhal jaenge...<br/>\n        Ilzam kitne lage pta nhi, par sajah to ek hi mil gyi...<br/>\n        Wakht se jab lagayi shart, tab asli aukat dikh gyi...<br/>\n        Manzil nhi jinhe op aise raston pe chal pade thhe...<br/>\n        Ab aa gyi to shayad dusra rasta chunn nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Puchhna mat hum kaise hai... bta nhi paenge...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Harkatein jo lagti thhi wo niyat bann gyi..<br/>\n        Dostike safar mein kyu chahat bann gyi...<br/>\n        Kaha thha ishq ho gya hai ab adat na bann jana... Badal nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Aapne khair mana nhi... ab smjha nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Ab puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Khuddar thhe hum shayad jab iska alam kiya...<br/>\n        Dildar thhe aap jab sath har dum diya...<br/>\n        Kahani aisi bann gyi ki adhuri keh nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Zid mat karna kyunki puri suna nhi paenge..<br/>\n        Puchhna mat hum kaise hai.. bta nhi paenge...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Pdhke ye sab aap ab bura na mann lena...<br/>\n        Man hi mann kuch yaad krke dil behla lena...<br/>\n        Kbhi nhi... aapko gum mein dekh nhi paenge...<br/>\n        Kbhi dikhe to kahise aakar hasa de jaenge...<br/>\n        Kbhi hue pehle ki tarah to ek hi bar gale mil jaenge...<br/>\n        Bs puchhna mat hum kaise hai... bta nhi paenge...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Don't ask how I am — I won't be able to say. It'll take time. This poem isn't blame — it's just truth. And someday, if we meet again, I'll just smile and hold you close.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":29,"id":"poem-29","title":"Tab Ki Ye Baat","subtitle":"That Was Then","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"That was then — when she existed in my world. Now the rains have dried, memories faded, tears too. But it was then when love was life itself.","searchText":"Poem 29 Tab Ki Ye Baat That Was Then Tab ki ye baat hai jab wo hua karti thhi... Dikhne mein achhi to wo thhi... mgar tarif humein mila krti thhi... Sath bde achhe lgte hai dono... duniya kaha krti thhi... Ab to sab asan hai... mushkilein to tab hua karti thhi... Uljhan ko suljhane ki bjay usme uljhneki adat hua krti thhi... Sukha to ab hai... baat to tab ki hai jab barish hua karti thhi... Do ke bjay ek chhata ye takad hua karti thhi.... Baat to tab ki hai jab mudkar dekhne ki wjah hua krti thhi... Ab to khair yaadein bhi dhundla gyi aur ansu bhi sukh gye... Baat tab ki hai jab mohbbt zindagi hua krti thhi... Suna raha hu kissa dil mein bsi yadon ka... Par baat to tab ki hai jab dilmein dhadkan hua karti thhi... Samne wo aur chehre par muskan hua krti thhi... Ji haan... tab ki ye baat hai jab wo hua karti thhi...! — ssp That was then — when she existed in my world. Now the rains have dried, memories faded, tears too. But it was then when love was life itself.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Tab ki ye baat hai jab wo hua karti thhi...<br/>\n        Dikhne mein achhi to wo thhi... mgar tarif humein mila krti thhi...<br/>\n        Sath bde achhe lgte hai dono... duniya kaha krti thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ab to sab asan hai... mushkilein to tab hua karti thhi...<br/>\n        Uljhan ko suljhane ki bjay usme uljhneki adat hua krti thhi...<br/>\n        Sukha to ab hai... baat to tab ki hai jab barish hua karti thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Do ke bjay ek chhata ye takad hua karti thhi....<br/>\n        Baat to tab ki hai jab mudkar dekhne ki wjah hua krti thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ab to khair yaadein bhi dhundla gyi aur ansu bhi sukh gye...<br/>\n        Baat tab ki hai jab mohbbt zindagi hua krti thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Suna raha hu kissa dil mein bsi yadon ka...<br/>\n        Par baat to tab ki hai jab dilmein dhadkan hua karti thhi...<br/>\n        Samne wo aur chehre par muskan hua krti thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ji haan... tab ki ye baat hai jab wo hua karti thhi...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">That was then — when she existed in my world. Now the rains have dried, memories faded, tears too. But it was then when love was life itself.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":30,"id":"poem-30","title":"The Dim Lights","subtitle":"An English Verse","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Two people in dim light, wondering if they'd be together forever. No words were needed. They relived memories, knew the journey was beautiful, and accepted the fight that lay ahead.","searchText":"Poem 30 The Dim Lights An English Verse The lights were dim, we sat together. Wondering will we be with each other, forever. It was dark back then and it's dark now, We weren't afraid before but we are by now. Guess it wasn't the absence of light — loneliness was the reason. Scary thing was the path, the life we had chosen. We were holding hands, no words were spoken. I guess they weren't necessary for the communication to happen. A conversation began, memories were relived. Golden days of life surely, each heart believed. Our journey was a success, experience was a delight. Two things lie ahead now, we knew — the future and the fight. We tried to sleep, to dream the life we wished. Moon did the rest, slowly the dream was accomplished. Stars were there, to add to the mystery. Prolonged the night became, going deep into the history. — ssp Two people in dim light, wondering if they'd be together forever. No words were needed. They relived memories, knew the journey was beautiful, and accepted the fight that lay ahead.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        The lights were dim, we sat together.<br/>\n        Wondering will we be with each other, forever.<br/>\n        It was dark back then and it's dark now,<br/>\n        We weren't afraid before but we are by now.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Guess it wasn't the absence of light — loneliness was the reason.<br/>\n        Scary thing was the path, the life we had chosen.<br/>\n        We were holding hands, no words were spoken.<br/>\n        I guess they weren't necessary for the communication to happen.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        A conversation began, memories were relived.<br/>\n        Golden days of life surely, each heart believed.<br/>\n        Our journey was a success, experience was a delight.<br/>\n        Two things lie ahead now, we knew — the future and the fight.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        We tried to sleep, to dream the life we wished.<br/>\n        Moon did the rest, slowly the dream was accomplished.<br/>\n        Stars were there, to add to the mystery.<br/>\n        Prolonged the night became, going deep into the history.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Two people in dim light, wondering if they'd be together forever. No words were needed. They relived memories, knew the journey was beautiful, and accepted the fight that lay ahead.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":31,"id":"poem-31","title":"Sapne Kanch Mein","subtitle":"Dreams in Glass","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Dreams locked behind glass, light peeking in secretly. Neither eyes nor mind could pull away — her face reflected on the glass in front.","searchText":"Poem 31 Sapne Kanch Mein Dreams in Glass Sapne thhe kanch mein band... Roshni chhupkese andar jhaak rahi thhi... Na ankhein hata paya na dhyan... Aapki surat jo samne sheeshe par chamakh rahi thhi... — ssp Dreams locked behind glass, light peeking in secretly. Neither eyes nor mind could pull away — her face reflected on the glass in front.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sapne thhe kanch mein band...<br/>\n        Roshni chhupkese andar jhaak rahi thhi...<br/>\n        Na ankhein hata paya na dhyan...<br/>\n        Aapki surat jo samne sheeshe par chamakh rahi thhi...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Dreams locked behind glass, light peeking in secretly. Neither eyes nor mind could pull away — her face reflected on the glass in front.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":32,"id":"poem-32","title":"Raat Mein Parchhai","subtitle":"Shadow at Night","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"At night there are no shadows — only depth. Without you, this sky holds only moonlight. Nothing more.","searchText":"Poem 32 Raat Mein Parchhai Shadow at Night Raat mein parchhai nhi hoti... Sirf gehrai hoti hai... Bina aapke iss aasman mein, Bs chandni hoti hai.... — ssp At night there are no shadows — only depth. Without you, this sky holds only moonlight. Nothing more.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Raat mein parchhai nhi hoti...<br/>\n        Sirf gehrai hoti hai...<br/>\n        Bina aapke iss aasman mein,<br/>\n        Bs chandni hoti hai....\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">At night there are no shadows — only depth. Without you, this sky holds only moonlight. Nothing more.</div>\n","featuredRank":7},{"number":33,"id":"poem-33","title":"Khoobsurati Aisi","subtitle":"Such Beauty","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Such beauty that you want to become a mirror for it; such a voice that you want to become the request. A love so precious it deserves to be guarded carefully.","searchText":"Poem 33 Khoobsurati Aisi Such Beauty Khoobsurati aisi... ki sheesha bnne ka dil karein, Pehchan aisi... ki parchhayi bnne ka dil karein, Likhawat aisi... ki kagaz bnne ka dil karein, Aur awaj aisi... ki guzaarish banne ka dil karein, Ek chahat aisi... ki adat banane ka dil karein, Ek muskan aisi ki bs amanat bnne ka dil karein, Aur amanat aisi rahein jiski hifazat karne ka dil karein! — ssp Such beauty that you want to become a mirror for it; such a voice that you want to become the request. A love so precious it deserves to be guarded carefully.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Khoobsurati aisi... ki sheesha bnne ka dil karein,<br/>\n        Pehchan aisi... ki parchhayi bnne ka dil karein,<br/>\n        Likhawat aisi... ki kagaz bnne ka dil karein,<br/>\n        Aur awaj aisi... ki guzaarish banne ka dil karein,\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ek chahat aisi... ki adat banane ka dil karein,<br/>\n        Ek muskan aisi ki bs amanat bnne ka dil karein,<br/>\n        Aur amanat aisi rahein jiski hifazat karne ka dil karein!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Such beauty that you want to become a mirror for it; such a voice that you want to become the request. A love so precious it deserves to be guarded carefully.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":34,"id":"poem-34","title":"Baat","subtitle":"Words Are Not Enough","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"To talk to you, feelings are enough — no words needed. For love, one meeting is enough — no togetherness required.","searchText":"Poem 34 Baat Words Are Not Enough Baat aapse karni hai to shabd nhi jazbaat kafi hai, Mohabbat ke liye sath kaha, bs ek hi mulakat kafi hai... — ssp To talk to you, feelings are enough — no words needed. For love, one meeting is enough — no togetherness required.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Baat aapse karni hai to shabd nhi jazbaat kafi hai,<br/>\n        Mohabbat ke liye sath kaha, bs ek hi mulakat kafi hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">To talk to you, feelings are enough — no words needed. For love, one meeting is enough — no togetherness required.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":35,"id":"poem-35","title":"एक रात थी वो ऐसी","subtitle":"Ek Raat Thi Wo Aisi","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"A man sat under stars, troubled but with a clear path ahead. He loved her, was a stranger at her door, gathered courage to confess — only to wake and find it was all a dream. Yet morning brought happiness: he had been charged with the crime of love.","searchText":"Poem 35 एक रात थी वो ऐसी Ek Raat Thi Wo Aisi एक रात थी वो ऐसी, सेहमी बारिश का अनुमान था, सितारोंके संग बैठा एक, मामूली सा इंसान था ...! पता नही कोनसी मुश्किल, जिससे वो परेशान था, मंजिल भी तो थी सामने, और रास्ता भी आसान था... ! चाहत थ��� उसकी जिसपर, हर कदर वो कुर्बान था, मगर उसके दर पर अबतक सिर्फ ये, अनजान सा मेहमान था ...! तो सोचा उसने बोल दू आखिर, पहला उसका प्यार था, इंकार की ना कोई गुंजाइश, जब साथ उसके संसार था...! इजहार वो आलम उसके, कोशिश का एक इनाम था, मगर राहत का वो सिलसिला, कमबख्त असलियत को इंकार था ...! आंख खुली तब सुलझा उसे, एक सपना था, हर बार था, अपने इस लाजमी चित्र का, वो खुद ही एक चित्रकार था ...! फिर भी सुबह दिल में उसके, एक खुशी का पैगाम था, इंसानियत के दरबार में उसपर, मोहब्बत का एक इल्जाम था... ! — ssp A man sat under stars, troubled but with a clear path ahead. He loved her, was a stranger at her door, gathered courage to confess — only to wake and find it was all a dream. Yet morning brought happiness: he had been charged with the crime of love.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        एक रात थी वो ऐसी, सेहमी बारिश का अनुमान था,<br/>\n        सितारोंके संग बैठा एक, मामूली सा इंसान था ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पता नही कोनसी मुश्किल, जिससे वो परेशान था,<br/>\n        मंजिल भी तो थी सामने, और रास्ता भी आसान था... !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        चाहत थ��� उसकी जिसपर, हर कदर वो कुर्बान था,<br/>\n        मगर उसके दर पर अबतक सिर्फ ये, अनजान सा मेहमान था ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        तो सोचा उसने बोल दू आखिर, पहला उसका प्यार था,<br/>\n        इंकार की ना कोई गुंजाइश, जब साथ उसके संसार था...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        इजहार वो आलम उसके, कोशिश का एक इनाम था,<br/>\n        मगर राहत का वो सिलसिला, कमबख्त असलियत को इंकार था ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आंख खुली तब सुलझा उसे, एक सपना था, हर बार था,<br/>\n        अपने इस लाजमी चित्र का, वो खुद ही एक चित्रकार था ...!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        फिर भी सुबह दिल में उसके, एक खुशी का पैगाम था,<br/>\n        इंसानियत के दरबार में उसपर, मोहब्बत का एक इल्जाम था... !\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A man sat under stars, troubled but with a clear path ahead. He loved her, was a stranger at her door, gathered courage to confess — only to wake and find it was all a dream. Yet morning brought happiness: he had been charged with the crime of love.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":36,"id":"poem-36","title":"For the Moment","subtitle":"An English Verse","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Whether it lasts a moment or becomes forever, love blooms in the castle we built together. The ship sailed far from shore; an evening whispered its secrets. Where to find such a smile again — eternity wonders.","searchText":"Poem 36 For the Moment An English Verse For the moment it lasts, or forever it may begin... Flirting in the castle, which we built together... Supporting this ship, which left the shores long ago... Making love underneath, the sparkling evening it whispered... Where to find such smile again... till eternity I wondered! — ssp Whether it lasts a moment or becomes forever, love blooms in the castle we built together. The ship sailed far from shore; an evening whispered its secrets. Where to find such a smile again — eternity wonders.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        For the moment it lasts,<br/>\n        or forever it may begin...<br/>\n        Flirting in the castle,<br/>\n        which we built together...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Supporting this ship,<br/>\n        which left the shores long ago...<br/>\n        Making love underneath,<br/>\n        the sparkling evening it whispered...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Where to find such smile again...<br/>\n        till eternity I wondered!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Whether it lasts a moment or becomes forever, love blooms in the castle we built together. The ship sailed far from shore; an evening whispered its secrets. Where to find such a smile again — eternity wonders.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":37,"id":"poem-37","title":"Your Harmony","subtitle":"An English Verse","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Your harmony lives with the moist air and the ocean. Be the light, be my beloved, fly for the moon — and let's meet wherever you land.","searchText":"Poem 37 Your Harmony An English Verse Your harmony is with the moist air... Ocean triumphs the worries which haunt you... Sunrise awakens a dream that lost you... Be the light and guide me through this journey... Be my beloved and fly for the moon... The place where you will land, Let's meet there soon! — ssp Your harmony lives with the moist air and the ocean. Be the light, be my beloved, fly for the moon — and let's meet wherever you land.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Your harmony is with the moist air...<br/>\n        Ocean triumphs the worries which haunt you...<br/>\n        Sunrise awakens a dream that lost you...<br/>\n        Be the light and guide me through this journey...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Be my beloved and fly for the moon...<br/>\n        The place where you will land,<br/>\n        Let's meet there soon!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Your harmony lives with the moist air and the ocean. Be the light, be my beloved, fly for the moon — and let's meet wherever you land.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":38,"id":"poem-38","title":"पण बहुतेक","subtitle":"Pan Bahuteka — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Only I had asked for love. The refusal was clear. In that foolish rush of feeling, friendship itself was lost — like a dewdrop sliding off a lotus leaf, carrying life's joy away.","searchText":"Poem 38 पण बहुतेक Pan Bahuteka — (Marathi) पण बहुतेक फक्त मीच होतो, ज्याने नेमकं प्रेम मागितलेलं ! नकार तो स्पष्ट होता, चेहऱ्यावर दुःख लपलेलं उगाच फसल्या भावनेच्या भरात, स्वतःचंच माकड करून घेतलेलं ! जास्त नाही पण थोडं तरी, वाईट मात्र वाटून गेलं अश्रूही आले भेटीला, मन हळवं गहिवरलेलं ! प्रेमाच्या त्या मूर्ख नादात, मैत्रीचं नातं ही संपून गेलं मोहक अश्या अळवावरच्या थेंबाने जणू जिवनातलं जगणं पळवून नेलं ! — ssp Only I had asked for love. The refusal was clear. In that foolish rush of feeling, friendship itself was lost — like a dewdrop sliding off a lotus leaf, carrying life's joy away.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पण बहुतेक फक्त मीच होतो, ज्याने नेमकं प्रेम मागितलेलं !<br/>\n        नकार तो स्पष्ट होता, चेहऱ्यावर दुःख लपलेलं<br/>\n        उगाच फसल्या भावनेच्या भरात, स्वतःचंच माकड करून घेतलेलं !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जास्त नाही पण थोडं तरी, वाईट मात्र वाटून गेलं<br/>\n        अश्रूही आले भेटीला, मन हळवं गहिवरलेलं !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        प्रेमाच्या त्या मूर्ख नादात, मैत्रीचं नातं ही संपून गेलं<br/>\n        मोहक अश्या अळवावरच्या थेंबाने जणू<br/>\n        जिवनातलं जगणं पळवून नेलं !\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Only I had asked for love. The refusal was clear. In that foolish rush of feeling, friendship itself was lost — like a dewdrop sliding off a lotus leaf, carrying life's joy away.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":39,"id":"poem-39","title":"Dhadkano Ka Haal Chahiye","subtitle":"The Heart Wants More Than Rules","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"The heart wants to know its beloved's heartbeat, not follow rules. Books and dreams matter more than rituals and destinations. All that's needed on the road is a friend's presence.","searchText":"Poem 39 Dhadkano Ka Haal Chahiye The Heart Wants More Than Rules Dhadkano ka haal chahiye, Faasion ki khabar nahi... Kitabon ke sheher chahiye, Riwazonki fikar nahi... Armaano ka mehel ho ek jarur, Khamoshi ka hunar nahi! Rastonpar dost ka ehsaas bas, Manzilon ki kadar nahi! — ssp The heart wants to know its beloved's heartbeat, not follow rules. Books and dreams matter more than rituals and destinations. All that's needed on the road is a friend's presence.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dhadkano ka haal chahiye,<br/>\n        Faasion ki khabar nahi...<br/>\n        Kitabon ke sheher chahiye,<br/>\n        Riwazonki fikar nahi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Armaano ka mehel ho ek jarur,<br/>\n        Khamoshi ka hunar nahi!<br/>\n        Rastonpar dost ka ehsaas bas,<br/>\n        Manzilon ki kadar nahi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The heart wants to know its beloved's heartbeat, not follow rules. Books and dreams matter more than rituals and destinations. All that's needed on the road is a friend's presence.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":40,"id":"poem-40","title":"Milne Ka Beshak","subtitle":"Meeting Was the Excuse","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Meeting you was just an excuse — the occasion was simply that. One wish was made, and you had to come and fulfil it. It was always meant to be.","searchText":"Poem 40 Milne Ka Beshak Meeting Was the Excuse Milne ka beshak, bahana hi thha... Mauka e vardaat, zamana hi thha... Humne toh bas, ek mannat mangi thhi, Puri karne aapko akhir, ana hi thha.... — ssp Meeting you was just an excuse — the occasion was simply that. One wish was made, and you had to come and fulfil it. It was always meant to be.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Milne ka beshak, bahana hi thha...<br/>\n        Mauka e vardaat, zamana hi thha...<br/>\n        Humne toh bas, ek mannat mangi thhi,<br/>\n        Puri karne aapko akhir, ana hi thha....\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Meeting you was just an excuse — the occasion was simply that. One wish was made, and you had to come and fulfil it. It was always meant to be.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":41,"id":"poem-41","title":"Galti Se Palke Jhuki","subtitle":"A Deep Sleep","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"When eyelids fall by accident, they don't rise easily again. When she gets upset once, there's no easy return. Like a deep sleep — it doesn't visit just anyone. A metaphor for emotional depth.","searchText":"Poem 41 Galti Se Palke Jhuki A Deep Sleep Galti se palke jhuki, toh asani se jaati nahi... Ek bar ruth gayi, toh koi jaam se aati nahi... Ameeron se dushmani jiski, gareeb ko satati nahi... Ye gehri nind hai janab, Har kisiko aazmaati nahi! — ssp When eyelids fall by accident, they don't rise easily again. When she gets upset once, there's no easy return. Like a deep sleep — it doesn't visit just anyone. A metaphor for emotional depth.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Galti se palke jhuki, toh asani se jaati nahi...<br/>\n        Ek bar ruth gayi, toh koi jaam se aati nahi...<br/>\n        Ameeron se dushmani jiski,<br/>\n        gareeb ko satati nahi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ye gehri nind hai janab,<br/>\n        Har kisiko aazmaati nahi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">When eyelids fall by accident, they don't rise easily again. When she gets upset once, there's no easy return. Like a deep sleep — it doesn't visit just anyone. A metaphor for emotional depth.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":42,"id":"poem-42","title":"Daag Toh Mil Gye","subtitle":"Found the Spots, Now Searching for the Moon","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"Found the spots on the moon, now searching for the moon itself. Found the flaws in passing moments — now looking for the speed at which they vanish.","searchText":"Poem 42 Daag Toh Mil Gye Found the Spots, Now Searching for the Moon Daag toh mil gye, ab chand dhund raha hu.... Lamhon ke guzarne ki, raftaar dhund raha hu! — ssp Found the spots on the moon, now searching for the moon itself. Found the flaws in passing moments — now looking for the speed at which they vanish.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Daag toh mil gye, ab chand dhund raha hu....<br/>\n        Lamhon ke guzarne ki, raftaar dhund raha hu!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Found the spots on the moon, now searching for the moon itself. Found the flaws in passing moments — now looking for the speed at which they vanish.</div>\n","featuredRank":12},{"number":43,"id":"poem-43","title":"Pass Rehne Ki Sifarish Nahi","subtitle":"No Request to Stay Close","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"No request to stay nearby — just a wish to see the moon together. Settle wherever you like, but don't forget to pass through my lane every now and then.","searchText":"Poem 43 Pass Rehne Ki Sifarish Nahi No Request to Stay Close Pass rehne ki sifarish nahi, bas chand dekhne ki guzaarish hai... Ghar kahin bhi basa lo janab, Bas gali se guzarna mat bhulna! — ssp No request to stay nearby — just a wish to see the moon together. Settle wherever you like, but don't forget to pass through my lane every now and then.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Pass rehne ki sifarish nahi,<br/>\n        bas chand dekhne ki guzaarish hai...<br/>\n        Ghar kahin bhi basa lo janab,<br/>\n        Bas gali se guzarna mat bhulna!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">No request to stay nearby — just a wish to see the moon together. Settle wherever you like, but don't forget to pass through my lane every now and then.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":44,"id":"poem-44","title":"Rang Bikhar Jaye Toh","subtitle":"When Colours Scatter","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},"meaning":"When colours scatter, the heart gets adorned. Like birds taking flight with the wind, the soul finds its wings.","searchText":"Poem 44 Rang Bikhar Jaye Toh When Colours Scatter Rang bikhar jaye toh, Dil sawar jayenge... Parindo ke lihaj se, Par sawar jayenge... — ssp When colours scatter, the heart gets adorned. Like birds taking flight with the wind, the soul finds its wings.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Rang bikhar jaye toh,<br/>\n        Dil sawar jayenge...<br/>\n        Parindo ke lihaj se,<br/>\n        Par sawar jayenge...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">When colours scatter, the heart gets adorned. Like birds taking flight with the wind, the soul finds its wings.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":45,"id":"poem-45","title":"Dost Hote Bde Ajeeb","subtitle":"Friends Are Strange","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"Friends are wonderfully strange — they celebrate and grieve together, know life's real fire, and are hard to find. A prayer: before our last rites, let us meet and embrace at least once.","searchText":"Poem 45 Dost Hote Bde Ajeeb Friends Are Strange Kuch baat hai jo kbhi byan hui nhi... Aj padhkar sunaunga... Dosti ka matlab thoda khulkar btaunga..! Dost hote bde ajeeb hai.... Awsar khushi ka ho ya gum ka... Ye to milkar hi maante hai... Janam din ho ya koi aur tyohar, Jashn saath hi mnana jante hai! Angaron ki asli aag to bs faqeer hi jaante hai... Apno se badhkar koi lage to unhe hum dost maante hai! Apas mein rota to koi nhi par hasana sab jaante hai... Mushkil se milte hai bhai dost aise... hum bhi jaante hai! Wapas mulaqat kbhi na ho payi unse to dua yehi karte hai... Janaze se pehle gale milne ki thodi fursat mangte hai! Kuch aise hai humare dost, kbhi jrur milaunga... Dosti ka matlab aur khulkar btaunga! — ssp Friends are wonderfully strange — they celebrate and grieve together, know life's real fire, and are hard to find. A prayer: before our last rites, let us meet and embrace at least once.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kuch baat hai jo kbhi byan hui nhi...<br/>\n        Aj padhkar sunaunga...<br/>\n        Dosti ka matlab thoda khulkar btaunga..!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dost hote bde ajeeb hai....<br/>\n        Awsar khushi ka ho ya gum ka...<br/>\n        Ye to milkar hi maante hai...<br/>\n        Janam din ho ya koi aur tyohar,<br/>\n        Jashn saath hi mnana jante hai!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Angaron ki asli aag to bs faqeer hi jaante hai...<br/>\n        Apno se badhkar koi lage to unhe hum dost maante hai!<br/>\n        Apas mein rota to koi nhi par hasana sab jaante hai...<br/>\n        Mushkil se milte hai bhai dost aise... hum bhi jaante hai!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wapas mulaqat kbhi na ho payi unse to dua yehi karte hai...<br/>\n        Janaze se pehle gale milne ki thodi fursat mangte hai!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kuch aise hai humare dost, kbhi jrur milaunga...<br/>\n        Dosti ka matlab aur khulkar btaunga!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Friends are wonderfully strange — they celebrate and grieve together, know life's real fire, and are hard to find. A prayer: before our last rites, let us meet and embrace at least once.</div>\n","featuredRank":4},{"number":46,"id":"poem-46","title":"पुराना ही था दोस्त","subtitle":"Purana Hi Tha Dost","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"An old friend rediscovered — since that meeting, even loneliness feels like conversation. You're not just a friend; you're family. Not a guest — you belong here.","searchText":"Poem 46 पुराना ही था दोस्त Purana Hi Tha Dost पुराना ही था दोस्त जिससे, नयी एक मुलाकात हुई है ... सच है ये की बाद उसके, हर तनहाई में भी बात हुई है ! शब्द खुद लिखते हैं हम, और धुन आपकी होती है ... मिलते ज्यादा हो नही, ये शिकायत हमारी होती है ! मानता हूं यार मैं, दोस्त है वो प्यार नही ... दोस्ती इतनी अच्छी हो तो, इससे बेहतर संसार नही! तारीफ नही करूंगा ज्यादा, इंसान हो भगवान नही ... इतना जरूर केह देता हूंकी, अपने हो, मेहमान नही ! बोल तो दिया सब, अब सिर्फ ये केहता हूं... हमेशा मिलते रहो तब, मुश्किल में जब रहता हूं! खूबसूरत तो आप हो ही, हमेशा बस खुशहाल रहो ... खिल उठें आप साथ जिसके, पास आपके, हमेशा वो इनसान रहो... खुशिया होंगी गम भी होंगे, बिलकूल ना परेशान रहो, हर लमहा एक छोटी ही सही पर चेहरे पर मुस्कान रहे! — ssp An old friend rediscovered — since that meeting, even loneliness feels like conversation. You're not just a friend; you're family. Not a guest — you belong here.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पुराना ही था दोस्त जिससे, नयी एक मुलाकात हुई है ...<br/>\n        सच है ये की बाद उसके, हर तनहाई में भी बात हुई है !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        शब्द खुद लिखते हैं हम, और धुन आपकी होती है ...<br/>\n        मिलते ज्यादा हो नही, ये शिकायत हमारी होती है !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        मानता हूं यार मैं, दोस्त है वो प्यार नही ...<br/>\n        दोस्ती इतनी अच्छी हो तो, इससे बेहतर संसार नही!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        तारीफ नही करूंगा ज्यादा, इंसान हो भगवान नही ...<br/>\n        इतना जरूर केह देता हूंकी, अपने हो, मेहमान नही !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        बोल तो दिया सब, अब सिर्फ ये केहता हूं...<br/>\n        हमेशा मिलते रहो तब, मुश्किल में जब रहता हूं!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        खूबसूरत तो आप हो ही, हमेशा बस खुशहाल रहो ...<br/>\n        खिल उठें आप साथ जिसके, पास आपके, हमेशा वो इनसान रहो...<br/>\n        खुशिया होंगी गम भी होंगे, बिलकूल ना परेशान रहो,<br/>\n        हर लमहा एक छोटी ही सही पर चेहरे पर मुस्कान रहे!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">An old friend rediscovered — since that meeting, even loneliness feels like conversation. You're not just a friend; you're family. Not a guest — you belong here.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":47,"id":"poem-47","title":"एका क्षणात","subtitle":"Eka Kshnat — In One Moment (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"In one moment, all memories appear. When birds leave, it sends a shiver. Friends give meaning to life by standing beside you in the difficult times.","searchText":"Poem 47 एका क्षणात Eka Kshnat — In One Moment (Marathi) एका क्षणात सगळ्या आठवणी, डोळ्यासमोर दर्शन देतात... पक्षी चाललेत उडून म्हंटल्यावर, अंगावरती शहारे येतात ... कठीण काळात मदत करून जे आपल्या झोळीत पुण्य घेतात... जीवन काय, जगतात सगळे, अर्थ त्याला मित्र देतात... — ssp In one moment, all memories appear. When birds leave, it sends a shiver. Friends give meaning to life by standing beside you in the difficult times.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        एका क्षणात सगळ्या आठवणी, डोळ्यासमोर दर्शन देतात...<br/>\n        पक्षी चाललेत उडून म्हंटल्यावर, अंगावरती शहारे येतात ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कठीण काळात मदत करून जे आपल्या झोळीत पुण्य घेतात...<br/>\n        जीवन काय, जगतात सगळे, अर्थ त्याला मित्र देतात...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">In one moment, all memories appear. When birds leave, it sends a shiver. Friends give meaning to life by standing beside you in the difficult times.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":48,"id":"poem-48","title":"Hua Pyar To","subtitle":"If There Was Love","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"If love happened, it will pass — we'll talk about it and tease a little too. That's friendship: you bring the paper, we'll colour it in.","searchText":"Poem 48 Hua Pyar To If There Was Love Hua pyar to jata denge, kuch tafleefein bata denge... Kuch aap kro gustakhi, thoda hum bhi sata denge... Dosti ki yehi to tasveer hai... Kagaj aap le aao bs, rangon se hum saja denge! — ssp If love happened, it will pass — we'll talk about it and tease a little too. That's friendship: you bring the paper, we'll colour it in.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Hua pyar to jata denge, kuch tafleefein bata denge...<br/>\n        Kuch aap kro gustakhi, thoda hum bhi sata denge...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dosti ki yehi to tasveer hai...<br/>\n        Kagaj aap le aao bs, rangon se hum saja denge!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">If love happened, it will pass — we'll talk about it and tease a little too. That's friendship: you bring the paper, we'll colour it in.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":49,"id":"poem-49","title":"Nikle Hai Khwabonka","subtitle":"Setting Out with Dreams","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"Setting out with a bag full of dreams, hoping life ahead will be better. A shared promise to move forward but not forget to look back, to keep doors open, and stay connected despite distance.","searchText":"Poem 49 Nikle Hai Khwabonka Setting Out with Dreams Nikle hai khwabonka baqsa lekar, jald hi ankhe khulengi... Guzre in dino se behtar, kash hi zindagi milegi... Koshish krenge aage badhkar pichhe mudna na bhulein, Kisi ko kbhi jarurat pde to mumkin har darwazein kholein... Apas mein anbann ho kbhi to wo darar na ban paye... Raste mein bhale doori rahein par kbhi anjann na bann jayein... Yehi mannat khuda se mangkar aage badh jate hai... Matlabi duniya ki kashmakash mein thoda apnapan laate hai! — ssp Setting out with a bag full of dreams, hoping life ahead will be better. A shared promise to move forward but not forget to look back, to keep doors open, and stay connected despite distance.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Nikle hai khwabonka baqsa lekar, jald hi ankhe khulengi...<br/>\n        Guzre in dino se behtar, kash hi zindagi milegi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Koshish krenge aage badhkar pichhe mudna na bhulein,<br/>\n        Kisi ko kbhi jarurat pde to mumkin har darwazein kholein...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Apas mein anbann ho kbhi to wo darar na ban paye...<br/>\n        Raste mein bhale doori rahein par kbhi anjann na bann jayein...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Yehi mannat khuda se mangkar aage badh jate hai...<br/>\n        Matlabi duniya ki kashmakash mein thoda apnapan laate hai!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Setting out with a bag full of dreams, hoping life ahead will be better. A shared promise to move forward but not forget to look back, to keep doors open, and stay connected despite distance.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":50,"id":"poem-50","title":"Azmane Se","subtitle":"On Testing Bonds","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"Testing reveals the true foundation of a bond — showing off does not. Even without a name, what we had was real. A closeness like rain on dry earth. Memories that poems bring back, every single time.","searchText":"Poem 50 Azmane Se On Testing Bonds Azmane se khul jati hai rishte ki buniyaad, itrane se nhi... Khokar bhi rehta hai har pal koi yaad, mit jaane se nhi... Shayad kuch bhi nhi thha humare beech... Par bina palak jhapke bheed mei bhi neeji batein hoti thhi... Wo ankhein yaad hai... batein yaad hai... Rishte ko naam nhi thha shayad par ehmiyat jrur thhi... Badahpan nhi, masumiyat jrur thhi... Na humne kbhi btaya na kisine puchha... Sukhi mitti ko sajane wali wo barish ki bund thhi... Hath tham kar baithta thha... duniya hi alag lagti thhi... Pta hai wo duniya meri nhi thhi par kasamse kafi khoob thhi... Rona bilkul nhi chahunga kbhi, par ant tak har kvita rula deti hai... Wo yaad, wo nazdiki, har gum bhula deti hai... Pichhe mudkar ab sab sapna lgta hai... Najane ab wapas kab nind ayein... — ssp Testing reveals the true foundation of a bond — showing off does not. Even without a name, what we had was real. A closeness like rain on dry earth. Memories that poems bring back, every single time.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Azmane se khul jati hai rishte ki buniyaad, itrane se nhi...<br/>\n        Khokar bhi rehta hai har pal koi yaad, mit jaane se nhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Shayad kuch bhi nhi thha humare beech...<br/>\n        Par bina palak jhapke bheed mei bhi neeji batein hoti thhi...<br/>\n        Wo ankhein yaad hai... batein yaad hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Rishte ko naam nhi thha shayad par ehmiyat jrur thhi...<br/>\n        Badahpan nhi, masumiyat jrur thhi...<br/>\n        Na humne kbhi btaya na kisine puchha...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sukhi mitti ko sajane wali wo barish ki bund thhi...<br/>\n        Hath tham kar baithta thha... duniya hi alag lagti thhi...<br/>\n        Pta hai wo duniya meri nhi thhi par kasamse kafi khoob thhi...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Rona bilkul nhi chahunga kbhi, par ant tak har kvita rula deti hai...<br/>\n        Wo yaad, wo nazdiki, har gum bhula deti hai...<br/>\n        Pichhe mudkar ab sab sapna lgta hai...<br/>\n        Najane ab wapas kab nind ayein...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Testing reveals the true foundation of a bond — showing off does not. Even without a name, what we had was real. A closeness like rain on dry earth. Memories that poems bring back, every single time.</div>\n","featuredRank":3},{"number":51,"id":"poem-51","title":"Jinho Ne Baat Karna","subtitle":"Choose Your Circle Carefully","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"Those who never learned to speak or never faced hardship — keep them at arm's length. Think carefully: the people alongside whom you became capable — keep them close.","searchText":"Poem 51 Jinho Ne Baat Karna Choose Your Circle Carefully Jinho ne baat karna bhi nahi seekha, Unse thhodi mulakat rakhenge... Na jinho ne mushkil wakht dekha, Unse thhodi jazbaat sikhenge... Ye badi ehem soochi hai yaron, Jara dhyan se chunna... Socho, sath jinke jeekar kabil bane hai hum, Unhe thhodi khudse durr rakhenge! — ssp Those who never learned to speak or never faced hardship — keep them at arm's length. Think carefully: the people alongside whom you became capable — keep them close.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Jinho ne baat karna bhi nahi seekha,<br/>\n        Unse thhodi mulakat rakhenge...<br/>\n        Na jinho ne mushkil wakht dekha,<br/>\n        Unse thhodi jazbaat sikhenge...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ye badi ehem soochi hai yaron,<br/>\n        Jara dhyan se chunna...<br/>\n        Socho, sath jinke jeekar kabil bane hai hum,<br/>\n        Unhe thhodi khudse durr rakhenge!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Those who never learned to speak or never faced hardship — keep them at arm's length. Think carefully: the people alongside whom you became capable — keep them close.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":52,"id":"poem-52","title":"Hum Dekhenge","subtitle":"We Shall See","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},"meaning":"Not children who only look forward, not old enough to only look back. Somewhere in between — young, figuring out how to balance relationships and responsibilities.","searchText":"Poem 52 Hum Dekhenge We Shall See Hum dekhenge! Bachhe nahi hai, jo bas aagey dekhenge... Budhe thodi hue, ki bas pichhe dekhenge... Beech kahin lakir kheechlo, bas wahin ke jawan hai hum... Rishte aur kam ka santulan, pata nahin hum kahase seekhenge! — ssp Not children who only look forward, not old enough to only look back. Somewhere in between — young, figuring out how to balance relationships and responsibilities.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Hum dekhenge!<br/>\n        Bachhe nahi hai, jo bas aagey dekhenge...<br/>\n        Budhe thodi hue, ki bas pichhe dekhenge...<br/>\n        Beech kahin lakir kheechlo,<br/>\n        bas wahin ke jawan hai hum...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Rishte aur kam ka santulan,<br/>\n        pata nahin hum kahase seekhenge!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Not children who only look forward, not old enough to only look back. Somewhere in between — young, figuring out how to balance relationships and responsibilities.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":53,"id":"poem-53","title":"Aai","subtitle":"For My Mother — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"rishtey","label":"Rishtey","description":"Family & bonds"},"meaning":"A son's tribute to his mother — she raised him, loves beyond herself, is both firm and gentle. Even a five-star meal can't match food from her hands. However tall he grows, he'll always be her little one.","searchText":"Poem 53 Aai For My Mother — (Marathi) जन्मापासून जीव लावला जिने, लहानाचं मोठं केलं ... प्रयत्नांची पराकाष्ठा करत, यशाच्या पायथ्याशी नेलं... स्वतःहून जास्त माया जिच्यावर, अशी ती एक...आई आहे... निश्शंक जिच्यात देव पाहतो, अशी विठ्ठल रखुमाई आहे... आजवरच्या कष्टांचं मोल, मी तरी तिला काय देणार... 5-स्टार च्या जेवणाला तरी, तिच्या हातची चव काय येणार... मोठं ही तिनेच केलं, तरी लहानही तीच समजते... अंतरमनात चालू असलेली लगबग, फक्त तिलाच उमजते... मजा मस्तीत पण शिस्त हवी, हाच तिचा उपदेश... बाबांना बिनशर्त साथ दिली, इतके वर्ष हे मात्र विशेष... थोडेही कुठे दुखावले तिला, तरी दिवसभर मनास लागते... कौतुकाची थाप जर मिळाली, तर आभाळ सुद्धा ठेंगणे वाटते... एवढेही शब्द पुरे आहेत, डोळ्यात तिच्या पाणी यायला... मोठा कितीही झालो तरी, लहान होईन कुशीत शिरायला... पन्नास पूर्ण झाली तशी, किमान शंभरी होऊन जाऊदे... स्वप्न असो वा झुंज सत्याशी, डोक्यावर फक्त तुझा हात राहूदे...! — ssp · (for Aai) A son's tribute to his mother — she raised him, loves beyond herself, is both firm and gentle. Even a five-star meal can't match food from her hands. However tall he grows, he'll always be her little one.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जन्मापासून जीव लावला जिने,<br/>\n        लहानाचं मोठं केलं ...<br/>\n        प्रयत्नांची पराकाष्ठा करत,<br/>\n        यशाच्या पायथ्याशी नेलं...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        स्वतःहून जास्त माया जिच्यावर,<br/>\n        अशी ती एक...आई आहे...<br/>\n        निश्शंक जिच्यात देव पाहतो,<br/>\n        अशी विठ्ठल रखुमाई आहे...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आजवरच्या कष्टांचं मोल,<br/>\n        मी तरी तिला काय देणार...<br/>\n        5-स्टार च्या जेवणाला तरी,<br/>\n        तिच्या हातची चव काय येणार...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        मोठं ही तिनेच केलं,<br/>\n        तरी लहानही तीच समजते...<br/>\n        अंतरमनात चालू असलेली लगबग,<br/>\n        फक्त तिलाच उमजते...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        मजा मस्तीत पण शिस्त हवी,<br/>\n        हाच तिचा उपदेश...<br/>\n        बाबांना बिनशर्त साथ दिली,<br/>\n        इतके वर्ष हे मात्र विशेष...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        थोडेही कुठे दुखावले तिला,<br/>\n        तरी दिवसभर मनास लागते...<br/>\n        कौतुकाची थाप जर मिळाली,<br/>\n        तर आभाळ सुद्धा ठेंगणे वाटते...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        एवढेही शब्द पुरे आहेत,<br/>\n        डोळ्यात तिच्या पाणी यायला...<br/>\n        मोठा कितीही झालो तरी,<br/>\n        लहान होईन कुशीत शिरायला...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पन्नास पूर्ण झाली तशी,<br/>\n        किमान शंभरी होऊन जाऊदे...<br/>\n        स्वप्न असो वा झुंज सत्याशी,<br/>\n        डोक्यावर फक्त तुझा हात राहूदे...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp  ·  (for Aai)</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A son's tribute to his mother — she raised him, loves beyond herself, is both firm and gentle. Even a five-star meal can't match food from her hands. However tall he grows, he'll always be her little one.</div>\n","featuredRank":19},{"number":54,"id":"poem-54","title":"Bhai","subtitle":"For My Brother — (Three Languages)","languages":["hindi","english","marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"rishtey","label":"Rishtey","description":"Family & bonds"},"meaning":"A brother described in three languages — first friend, best memory, teacher of mischief and wisdom. My closet has more of his clothes than mine. However tall I grow, I'll always be your younger brother.","searchText":"Poem 54 Bhai For My Brother — (Three Languages) Aasan nahi hai bhai ke rishte ko, ek hi bhasha mein samjhana, Isliye teen mein koshish karunga, kuch anuman lage to batana! in english — Who was my first friend? Whom did I tell the stories to? It's good that just one guy Is answer to all the questions, phew! He saw me grow up, those memories will never be torn, He's the best thing ever happened to me, even before I was born! खरंतर — मजा मस्ती वगैरे अगदी, सगळं त्यानेच शिकवलं काय करावं नि काय करू नये, हे नेहमी त्यानेच दाखवलं ! माझ्या कपाटात माझे स्वतःचे कमी, त्याचेच कपडे जास्त आहेत, इतर कोणा पेक्षाही घरात, याचेच नखरे जास्त आहेत! bas — Kya batau aur jyada, janamdin ki badhai ho! Har pal jiyenge zindagi ka jismein, aapki khushi samayi ho! Keh to diya sab, ab sirf akhir mein ye kahunga, Kitna bhi bada ho jau hmesha, tumhara chhota bhai hi rahunga...! — सौ. A brother described in three languages — first friend, best memory, teacher of mischief and wisdom. My closet has more of his clothes than mine. However tall I grow, I'll always be your younger brother.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\" style=\"font-style:italic; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px;\">\n        Aasan nahi hai bhai ke rishte ko, ek hi bhasha mein samjhana,<br/>\n        Isliye teen mein koshish karunga, kuch anuman lage to batana!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n<em>in english —</em><br/>\n        Who was my first friend? Whom did I tell the stories to?<br/>\n        It's good that just one guy<br/>\n        Is answer to all the questions, phew!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        He saw me grow up, those memories will never be torn,<br/>\n        He's the best thing ever happened to me, even before I was born!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\" style=\"margin-top:20px;\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n<em style=\"font-style:italic; color:var(--muted);\">खरंतर —</em><br/>\n        मजा मस्ती वगैरे अगदी, सगळं त्यानेच शिकवलं<br/>\n        काय करावं नि काय करू नये, हे नेहमी त्यानेच दाखवलं !\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        माझ्या कपाटात माझे स्वतःचे कमी, त्याचेच कपडे जास्त आहेत,<br/>\n        इतर कोणा पेक्षाही घरात, याचेच नखरे जास्त आहेत!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-body\" style=\"margin-top:20px;\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n<em style=\"color:var(--muted);\">bas —</em><br/>\n        Kya batau aur jyada, janamdin ki badhai ho!<br/>\n        Har pal jiyenge zindagi ka jismein, aapki khushi samayi ho!<br/>\n        Keh to diya sab, ab sirf akhir mein ye kahunga,<br/>\n        Kitna bhi bada ho jau hmesha, tumhara chhota bhai hi rahunga...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— सौ.</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A brother described in three languages — first friend, best memory, teacher of mischief and wisdom. My closet has more of his clothes than mine. However tall I grow, I'll always be your younger brother.</div>\n","featuredRank":9},{"number":55,"id":"poem-55","title":"Jinhone Bolna Sikhaya","subtitle":"Those Who Taught Me to Speak","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"rishtey","label":"Rishtey","description":"Family & bonds"},"meaning":"Those who taught him to speak — now he can't find words to speak to them. Those who were once the reason for laughter — no meetings happen anymore. Grown up, yet still needing a parent's warmth.","searchText":"Poem 55 Jinhone Bolna Sikhaya Those Who Taught Me to Speak जिन्होंने बोलना सिखाया, उनसे बात नहीं होती... जो कभी हसने की वजह थे, उनसे मुलाकात नहीं होती... जीना है तो जी भी देंगे, इतने कमजोर थोडी है मगर... बड़े होकर भी ऐसा नहीं है की, मां बाप के प्यार की दरख्वास्त नहीं होती... — ssp Those who taught him to speak — now he can't find words to speak to them. Those who were once the reason for laughter — no meetings happen anymore. Grown up, yet still needing a parent's warmth.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जिन्होंने बोलना सिखाया,<br/>\n        उनसे बात नहीं होती...<br/>\n        जो कभी हसने की वजह थे,<br/>\n        उनसे मुलाकात नहीं होती...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जीना है तो जी भी देंगे,<br/>\n        इतने कमजोर थोडी है मगर...<br/>\n        बड़े होकर भी ऐसा नहीं है की,<br/>\n        मां बाप के प्यार की दरख्वास्त नहीं होती...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Those who taught him to speak — now he can't find words to speak to them. Those who were once the reason for laughter — no meetings happen anymore. Grown up, yet still needing a parent's warmth.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":56,"id":"poem-56","title":"Kalam","subtitle":"The Pen","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"The pen kept writing and life kept living. Some hands taught him how to write; others taught him how to live.","searchText":"Poem 56 Kalam The Pen कलम लिखती गयी, और हम जीते गये... कुछ हाथोंने लिखना सिखा दिया, कुछ ने जीना... ! — ssp The pen kept writing and life kept living. Some hands taught him how to write; others taught him how to live.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कलम लिखती गयी, और हम जीते गये...<br/>\n        कुछ हाथोंने लिखना सिखा दिया, कुछ ने जीना... !\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The pen kept writing and life kept living. Some hands taught him how to write; others taught him how to live.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":57,"id":"poem-57","title":"स्वप्नातील सुख","subtitle":"Swapnatil Sukh — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"A young man searching for happiness and connection. Haunted by the future, careful with each step. He stumbles, loses his way — but from failure and experience, a successful person is quietly emerging.","searchText":"Poem 57 स्वप्नातील सुख Swapnatil Sukh — (Marathi) स्वप्नातील सुख आणि नात्यांतील सहवास तो शोधतोय... अनेक दिवसांनी आज मनातलं, मोजकं काही बोलतोय... त्यास भविष्याचं भूत आणि वर्तमानाचा विचार कायम सलतोय... अपेक्षांच्या ओझ्यापायी प्रत्येक पायरी तो जरा जपूनच चढतोय... वाटचालीत धडपडतोय, मधेच वाट सुद्धा हरवतोय... अपयश आणि अनुभवांतून मात्र कदाचित, एक यशस्वी व्यक्तिमत्व उलगडतंय... गोष्ट त्या मुलाची आहे, जो career साठी झगडतोय... उद्याच्या आयुष्यासाठी जरासा, आज जगायला विसरतोय... कोऱ्या कागदाचा वैमानिक, थेट क्षितिजा पलीकडे उडू पाहतोय... नव्या रंगानिशी बाहेर पडलेला, हा चित्रकारच बदलतोय...! — ssp A young man searching for happiness and connection. Haunted by the future, careful with each step. He stumbles, loses his way — but from failure and experience, a successful person is quietly emerging.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        स्वप्नातील सुख आणि नात्यांतील सहवास तो शोधतोय...<br/>\n        अनेक दिवसांनी आज मनातलं, मोजकं काही बोलतोय...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        त्यास भविष्याचं भूत आणि वर्तमानाचा विचार कायम सलतोय...<br/>\n        अपेक्षांच्या ओझ्यापायी प्रत्येक पायरी तो जरा जपूनच चढतोय...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        वाटचालीत धडपडतोय, मधेच वाट सुद्धा हरवतोय...<br/>\n        अपयश आणि अनुभवांतून मात्र कदाचित, एक यशस्वी व्यक्तिमत्व उलगडतंय...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        गोष्ट त्या मुलाची आहे, जो career साठी झगडतोय...<br/>\n        उद्याच्या आयुष्यासाठी जरासा, आज जगायला विसरतोय...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कोऱ्या कागदाचा वैमानिक, थेट क्षितिजा पलीकडे उडू पाहतोय...<br/>\n        नव्या रंगानिशी बाहेर पडलेला, हा चित्रकारच बदलतोय...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A young man searching for happiness and connection. Haunted by the future, careful with each step. He stumbles, loses his way — but from failure and experience, a successful person is quietly emerging.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":58,"id":"poem-58","title":"Udyachich Chinta","subtitle":"Tomorrow's Worry — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Why does worry about tomorrow consume today? Which hope remains to dream upon? A universal ache — anxiety about the future quietly eating the present.","searchText":"Poem 58 Udyachich Chinta Tomorrow's Worry — (Marathi) Udyachich chinta, kay re bhagwanta... Ajche hi diwas kalchya athwanit ch jawe? Kay hi dasha, Ann kuthli ti disha, Sang tuch ya bhiti poti kse me nijawe? Hach sarwancha wichar, rog ituka kay upchar, Kuthlya ashewar ata ekhade swapn tri bghawe? — ssp Why does worry about tomorrow consume today? Which hope remains to dream upon? A universal ache — anxiety about the future quietly eating the present.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Udyachich chinta, kay re bhagwanta...<br/>\n        Ajche hi diwas kalchya athwanit ch jawe?<br/>\n        Kay hi dasha, Ann kuthli ti disha,<br/>\n        Sang tuch ya bhiti poti kse me nijawe?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Hach sarwancha wichar, rog ituka kay upchar,<br/>\n        Kuthlya ashewar ata ekhade swapn tri bghawe?\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Why does worry about tomorrow consume today? Which hope remains to dream upon? A universal ache — anxiety about the future quietly eating the present.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":59,"id":"poem-59","title":"Kuch Kami","subtitle":"The Art of Living with Less","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Living with some shortage is a skill; laughing through some pain is grace. Knowing someone's wish before they say it — that's art. A gentle observation about resilience and quiet attentiveness.","searchText":"Poem 59 Kuch Kami The Art of Living with Less Kuch kami k sath jeena ek hunar hai... Kuch nami k sath hasna ek ada hai... Khwaishonki kaifiyat puchhna... achha hai... Par bin bataye usey janna ek kala hai... कुछ कमी के साथ जीना, एक हुनर है... कुछ नमी के साथ हसना, एक अदा है... ख्वाइशों की कैफियत पूछना, तो अच्छा है, पर बिन बताएं उन्हे जानना भी, एक कला है...! — ssp Living with some shortage is a skill; laughing through some pain is grace. Knowing someone's wish before they say it — that's art. A gentle observation about resilience and quiet attentiveness.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Kuch kami k sath jeena ek hunar hai...<br/>\n          Kuch nami k sath hasna ek ada hai...<br/>\n          Khwaishonki kaifiyat puchhna... achha hai...<br/>\n          Par bin bataye usey janna ek kala hai...\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          कुछ कमी के साथ जीना, एक हुनर है...<br/>\n          कुछ नमी के साथ हसना, एक अदा है...<br/>\n          ख्वाइशों की कैफियत पूछना, तो अच्छा है,<br/>\n          पर बिन बताएं उन्हे जानना भी, एक कला है...!\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Living with some shortage is a skill; laughing through some pain is grace. Knowing someone's wish before they say it — that's art. A gentle observation about resilience and quiet attentiveness.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":60,"id":"poem-60","title":"Kavita Mein Shabd","subtitle":"Words in a Poem","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Words alone are incomplete in a poem — they need a melody. A memory tied to a song is impossible to forget. Some cry, others give thanks — the same music, different lives. Live openly, not just thoughtfully.","searchText":"Poem 60 Kavita Mein Shabd Words in a Poem कविता में, \"शब्द\" ये एक ही पहलू है... कभी कभी अधुरा पड जाता है... पर जब धुन उसे मिलती है, तब सूर से जज़्बात जुड़ते है... छुपे हो कहीं एहसेस अलग से, तो ढूंढने थोडी पड़ते है ... याद जुड़ी हो किसी ऐसेही गानेसे, तो भूलना बड़ा मुश्किल ... अक्सर कोई चलता है, तब गुजरा लम्हा याद आ जाता है ... बस कुछ पल बिताएं जिनपर, उन्हे फिरसे सामने लाता है ... शब्द वही, धुन भी समान... बस हालात बदलें होते हैं... कोई फूट के रोता है, तो कोई दूजा शुकर मनाता है... सोचकर बिताना नहीं इसे... खुलकर जीना होता है ... — ssp Words alone are incomplete in a poem — they need a melody. A memory tied to a song is impossible to forget. Some cry, others give thanks — the same music, different lives. Live openly, not just thoughtfully.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कविता में, \"शब्द\" ये एक ही पहलू है...<br/>\n        कभी कभी अधुरा पड जाता है...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पर जब धुन उसे मिलती है,<br/>\n        तब सूर से जज़्बात जुड़ते है...<br/>\n        छुपे हो कहीं एहसेस अलग से,<br/>\n        तो ढूंढने थोडी पड़ते है ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        याद जुड़ी हो किसी ऐसेही गानेसे,<br/>\n        तो भूलना बड़ा मुश्किल ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        अक्सर कोई चलता है, तब गुजरा लम्हा याद आ जाता है ...<br/>\n        बस कुछ पल बिताएं जिनपर, उन्हे फिरसे सामने लाता है ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        शब्द वही, धुन भी समान...<br/>\n        बस हालात बदलें होते हैं...<br/>\n        कोई फूट के रोता है, तो कोई दूजा शुकर मनाता है...<br/>\n        सोचकर बिताना नहीं इसे...<br/>\n        खुलकर जीना होता है ...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Words alone are incomplete in a poem — they need a melody. A memory tied to a song is impossible to forget. Some cry, others give thanks — the same music, different lives. Live openly, not just thoughtfully.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":61,"id":"poem-61","title":"Sangeet","subtitle":"Music & Memory","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"A familiar song triggers a memory — just one day spent together, but the music carries that person back. Some cry, some give thanks. The same tune, different lives, different feeling.","searchText":"Poem 61 Sangeet Music & Memory Aksar jab koi chalata hai, Wo guzra lamha yaad aa jata hai... Bas ek hi din bitaya jispar, Usey phirse samne lata hai... Sangeet wohi, dhun bhi saman, Bas halaat badal jatein hai... Koi fut ke rota hai, to koi duja shukar manata hai... Sochkar beetana nhi, isey to khulkar jeena hota hai... — ssp A familiar song triggers a memory — just one day spent together, but the music carries that person back. Some cry, some give thanks. The same tune, different lives, different feeling.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Aksar jab koi chalata hai,<br/>\n        Wo guzra lamha yaad aa jata hai...<br/>\n        Bas ek hi din bitaya jispar,<br/>\n        Usey phirse samne lata hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sangeet wohi, dhun bhi saman,<br/>\n        Bas halaat badal jatein hai...<br/>\n        Koi fut ke rota hai, to koi duja shukar manata hai...<br/>\n        Sochkar beetana nhi, isey to khulkar jeena hota hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A familiar song triggers a memory — just one day spent together, but the music carries that person back. Some cry, some give thanks. The same tune, different lives, different feeling.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":62,"id":"poem-62","title":"In Quest","subtitle":"On Identity — A Prose Reflection","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"In trying to become someone else, we lose ourselves. Grow as a unique identity — not as a copy of someone who is already great.","searchText":"Poem 62 In Quest On Identity — A Prose Reflection In quest of trying to be like somebody, we always forget that eventually we were made unique. This quest takes us away from our own identity. When we completely transform and reach our destination in that quest, become somebody significant — congratulations, your own self isn't left much now. So try to grow as a unique identity, not to mold into an already developed stature. — ssp In trying to become someone else, we lose ourselves. Grow as a unique identity — not as a copy of someone who is already great.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        In quest of trying to be like somebody, we always forget that eventually we were made unique. This quest takes us away from our own identity. When we completely transform and reach our destination in that quest, become somebody significant — congratulations, your own self isn't left much now.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        So try to grow as a unique identity,<br/>\n        not to mold into an already developed stature.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">In trying to become someone else, we lose ourselves. Grow as a unique identity — not as a copy of someone who is already great.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":63,"id":"poem-63","title":"Halat Ne Majbur","subtitle":"Life Made Me a Craftsman","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Life and circumstances forged this skill — craftsmanship was never learned easily. In both Hindi and Marathi, the message is the same: our struggles made us who we are.","searchText":"Poem 63 Halat Ne Majbur Life Made Me a Craftsman Halat ne majbur bana diya, Aur zindagi ne majdur... Karagiri hum aise hi nhi sikhe janab... हालात ने मजबूर बना दिया, और जिंदगी ने मजदूर... कारागिरी हम ऐसेही नही सीखे जनाब...! — ssp Life and circumstances forged this skill — craftsmanship was never learned easily. In both Hindi and Marathi, the message is the same: our struggles made us who we are.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Halat ne majbur bana diya,<br/>\n          Aur zindagi ne majdur...<br/>\n          Karagiri hum aise hi nhi sikhe janab...\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          हालात ने मजबूर बना दिया,<br/>\n          और जिंदगी ने मजदूर...<br/>\n          कारागिरी हम ऐसेही नही सीखे जनाब...!\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Life and circumstances forged this skill — craftsmanship was never learned easily. In both Hindi and Marathi, the message is the same: our struggles made us who we are.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":64,"id":"poem-64","title":"Agar Sab Hi Ki Ruh","subtitle":"If All Souls Are One","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"If all souls are connected, why does everyone live such a separate life? A philosophical question about the contradiction between spiritual oneness and the reality of lived isolation.","searchText":"Poem 64 Agar Sab Hi Ki Ruh If All Souls Are One Agar sab hi ki ruh ek sath judi hai... To kyun hmare samne alag zindagi padi hai? अगर सब ही की रूह एक साथ जुड़ी है... तो क्यू हमारे सामने अलग अलग जिंदगी पड़ी है? — ssp If all souls are connected, why does everyone live such a separate life? A philosophical question about the contradiction between spiritual oneness and the reality of lived isolation.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Agar sab hi ki ruh ek sath judi hai...<br/>\n          To kyun hmare samne alag zindagi padi hai?\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          अगर सब ही की रूह एक साथ जुड़ी है...<br/>\n          तो क्यू हमारे सामने अलग अलग जिंदगी पड़ी है?\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">If all souls are connected, why does everyone live such a separate life? A philosophical question about the contradiction between spiritual oneness and the reality of lived isolation.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":65,"id":"poem-65","title":"Bekhudi","subtitle":"On Purpose","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Are you even aware of your own selflessness? Then for whom are you living? The answer isn't simple — but the entire universe is waiting for you to know your purpose.","searchText":"Poem 65 Bekhudi On Purpose Bekhudi se wakif ho, To kiske liye jiyein jaa rahein ho... Jawab asan to hai nahin, Maqsaad janne puri kaynaat khadi hai... — ssp Are you even aware of your own selflessness? Then for whom are you living? The answer isn't simple — but the entire universe is waiting for you to know your purpose.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Bekhudi se wakif ho,<br/>\n        To kiske liye jiyein jaa rahein ho...<br/>\n        Jawab asan to hai nahin,<br/>\n        Maqsaad janne puri kaynaat khadi hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Are you even aware of your own selflessness? Then for whom are you living? The answer isn't simple — but the entire universe is waiting for you to know your purpose.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":66,"id":"poem-66","title":"Laksh","subtitle":"After Success, What?","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Work hard to reach your goal — that's the easy answer. The real question is what comes after success? What do you pursue once you've achieved what you set out for?","searchText":"Poem 66 Laksh After Success, What? Laksh paane ke liye mehnat karo! Ye to bada asan jawab hai... Asal mein safalta ke baad kya? Ye bada umda sawal hai... — ssp Work hard to reach your goal — that's the easy answer. The real question is what comes after success? What do you pursue once you've achieved what you set out for?","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Laksh paane ke liye mehnat karo!<br/>\n        Ye to bada asan jawab hai...<br/>\n        Asal mein safalta ke baad kya?<br/>\n        Ye bada umda sawal hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Work hard to reach your goal — that's the easy answer. The real question is what comes after success? What do you pursue once you've achieved what you set out for?</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":67,"id":"poem-67","title":"Mar Gye","subtitle":"On Death & Blame","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"The dead feel nothing — it's those who remain who suffer. Don't blame death; blame life for its cruelties. Death, in the end, is innocent.","searchText":"Poem 67 Mar Gye On Death & Blame Mar gye usey nhi... reh gye unhe taqleef hai... Zindagi ko kosiye janab... maut to badi nirdosh hai.... — ssp The dead feel nothing — it's those who remain who suffer. Don't blame death; blame life for its cruelties. Death, in the end, is innocent.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Mar gye usey nhi... reh gye unhe taqleef hai...<br/>\n        Zindagi ko kosiye janab... maut to badi nirdosh hai....\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The dead feel nothing — it's those who remain who suffer. Don't blame death; blame life for its cruelties. Death, in the end, is innocent.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":68,"id":"poem-68","title":"Wakht Nhi Badal Raha","subtitle":"Change Everything","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"If time won't change, change yourself. If your identity feels stuck, change your name. Everything is changeable — because when you change yourself, the world changes too.","searchText":"Poem 68 Wakht Nhi Badal Raha Change Everything Wakht nhi badal raha to aap badal do... Pehchan nhi badal rahi to naam badal lo... Din nahin katt raha to kaam badal do... Raat nahin guzar rahi to jaam badal lo... Manzil nahin mil rahi to inaam badal do... Mannatein hi puri na ho to bhagwan badal lo... Khudko badalna hai to apni duniya badal do... Duniya ko badalna hai to pehle khudko badal lo... — ssp If time won't change, change yourself. If your identity feels stuck, change your name. Everything is changeable — because when you change yourself, the world changes too.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wakht nhi badal raha to aap badal do...<br/>\n        Pehchan nhi badal rahi to naam badal lo...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Din nahin katt raha to kaam badal do...<br/>\n        Raat nahin guzar rahi to jaam badal lo...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Manzil nahin mil rahi to inaam badal do...<br/>\n        Mannatein hi puri na ho to bhagwan badal lo...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Khudko badalna hai to apni duniya badal do...<br/>\n        Duniya ko badalna hai to pehle khudko badal lo...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">If time won't change, change yourself. If your identity feels stuck, change your name. Everything is changeable — because when you change yourself, the world changes too.</div>\n","featuredRank":8},{"number":69,"id":"poem-69","title":"Laugh Out","subtitle":"On Strength","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Laugh with people, cry alone. Show strength, ignore small provocations, stay positive. One day, you will be known — for a genuinely good reason.","searchText":"Poem 69 Laugh Out On Strength Laugh out with ppl, but do cry alone... People will admire, the strong will you have shown... Don't pick the small things, the pitty looks people have thrown... Just focus on the positives, surely their minds will be blown... Continue with this process, maintain a polite tone... And one day my friend, For a good reason you will be known! — ssp Laugh with people, cry alone. Show strength, ignore small provocations, stay positive. One day, you will be known — for a genuinely good reason.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Laugh out with ppl, but do cry alone...<br/>\n        People will admire, the strong will you have shown...<br/>\n        Don't pick the small things, the pitty looks people have thrown...<br/>\n        Just focus on the positives, surely their minds will be blown...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Continue with this process, maintain a polite tone...<br/>\n        And one day my friend,<br/>\n        For a good reason you will be known!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Laugh with people, cry alone. Show strength, ignore small provocations, stay positive. One day, you will be known — for a genuinely good reason.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":70,"id":"poem-70","title":"Janam Din","subtitle":"The Dream of Living","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"A birthday feels like a festival, and friendship deepens a little more. The most beautiful dream is the one felt after truly living. Sleep deeply when the people you love are near.","searchText":"Poem 70 Janam Din The Dream of Living Janam din, tyohar jaisa, aaj kuch sama thha... Dosti ka khumar aj thoda, hadd se aagey badha thha... Haseen sabse khwab jiska, jeeneke baad ehsas ho... Nind ayein khoob gehri, kal jab apne pass ho... हसीन सबसे, ख्वाब जिसका, जीनेके बाद एहसास हो... नींद आएं खूब गेहरी, कल जब अपने पास हो ...! — ssp A birthday feels like a festival, and friendship deepens a little more. The most beautiful dream is the one felt after truly living. Sleep deeply when the people you love are near.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Janam din, tyohar jaisa, aaj kuch sama thha...<br/>\n          Dosti ka khumar aj thoda, hadd se aagey badha thha...\n        </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Haseen sabse khwab jiska, jeeneke baad ehsas ho...<br/>\n          Nind ayein khoob gehri, kal jab apne pass ho...\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          हसीन सबसे, ख्वाब जिसका,<br/>\n          जीनेके बाद एहसास हो...<br/>\n          नींद आएं खूब गेहरी,<br/>\n          कल जब अपने पास हो ...!\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A birthday feels like a festival, and friendship deepens a little more. The most beautiful dream is the one felt after truly living. Sleep deeply when the people you love are near.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":71,"id":"poem-71","title":"जवानी की उम्र","subtitle":"Jawani Ki Umar — The Age of Youth","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"In youth, there's a somewhat absurd romance in every struggle, a hidden simplicity in every skill. Decisions shift as you learn to respect age; relationships are sustained by recognising their worth.","searchText":"Poem 71 जवानी की उम्र Jawani Ki Umar — The Age of Youth दर बदर की कश्मकश में, बेतुकी सी आशिकी है ... हर हुनर के एक सफर में, एक छुपी सी सादगी है ... उम्र का लिहाज करते ही, फैसले की बुनियाद बदलती है ... और एहमियत को जाननेसे ही, रिश्ते की फर्याद समहलती है ...! — ssp In youth, there's a somewhat absurd romance in every struggle, a hidden simplicity in every skill. Decisions shift as you learn to respect age; relationships are sustained by recognising their worth.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        दर बदर की कश्मकश में,<br/>\n        बेतुकी सी आशिकी है ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        हर हुनर के एक सफर में,<br/>\n        एक छुपी सी सादगी है ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        उम्र का लिहाज करते ही,<br/>\n        फैसले की बुनियाद बदलती है ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        और एहमियत को जाननेसे ही,<br/>\n        रिश्ते की फर्याद समहलती है ...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">In youth, there's a somewhat absurd romance in every struggle, a hidden simplicity in every skill. Decisions shift as you learn to respect age; relationships are sustained by recognising their worth.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":72,"id":"poem-72","title":"Apnepan","subtitle":"On Belonging","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Belonging is hard to measure; a worried father's feelings — impossible to describe. No clear destination, no easy road — yet this stubborn human keeps walking to find an identity in an unknown world.","searchText":"Poem 72 Apnepan On Belonging Apnepan ka paimana mushkil... Pareshan pitaji ki kaifiyat namumkin... Na manzil mumkin hai, Na rasta asan... Bawjood nikal pada hai tey karne, Ye khudgarz insan... Kuch saal jo dharti par, Hai sirf ek mamuli mehman... Kya pta kyu dhund raha hai, Anjan duniya mein ek khudki pehchan... — ssp Belonging is hard to measure; a worried father's feelings — impossible to describe. No clear destination, no easy road — yet this stubborn human keeps walking to find an identity in an unknown world.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Apnepan ka paimana mushkil...<br/>\n        Pareshan pitaji ki kaifiyat namumkin...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Na manzil mumkin hai,<br/>\n        Na rasta asan...<br/>\n        Bawjood nikal pada hai tey karne,<br/>\n        Ye khudgarz insan...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kuch saal jo dharti par,<br/>\n        Hai sirf ek mamuli mehman...<br/>\n        Kya pta kyu dhund raha hai,<br/>\n        Anjan duniya mein ek khudki pehchan...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Belonging is hard to measure; a worried father's feelings — impossible to describe. No clear destination, no easy road — yet this stubborn human keeps walking to find an identity in an unknown world.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":73,"id":"poem-73","title":"Zindagi Adhuri","subtitle":"Life Is Incomplete","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Life is incomplete — not love. Love, for every person, is whole and enough. But the world and its structures remain unfinished.","searchText":"Poem 73 Zindagi Adhuri Life Is Incomplete Zindagi adhuri hai dost, pyar nhi... Ishq to har ek mukammal hai, magar ye sansar nhi! — ssp Life is incomplete — not love. Love, for every person, is whole and enough. But the world and its structures remain unfinished.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Zindagi adhuri hai dost, pyar nhi...<br/>\n        Ishq to har ek mukammal hai, magar ye sansar nhi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Life is incomplete — not love. Love, for every person, is whole and enough. But the world and its structures remain unfinished.</div>\n","featuredRank":20},{"number":74,"id":"poem-74","title":"Wakht","subtitle":"Time","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Everyone has many thoughts but no time. Everyone speaks but no one listens. Art flourishes but audiences disappear. Relationships soften but distances deepen. We all live under the same sky but feel rootless. We'll change things — but later, because time is never with us.","searchText":"Poem 74 Wakht Time Insan kayin, bas dikkat yahin hai, Ki wakht kisike pass nahin hai... Sochte sab, khwaishein nayin hai, Bin badal kisi ne barsaat sahi hai... Sab bolte jarur, par sirf sunta to koi nahi hai, Wakht jo kisike, pass nahin hai... Ganomein dhun badli jarur, Par kavita ke alfaz wohi hai... Rachanatmak kalakar jarur, jaankar aj shrota nahi hai, Wakht jo kisike, pass nahin hai... Rishton mein narmai jarur, Par faasion ki gehrai rahi hai... Ehmiyaat ka sheesha saamne rakhe bina, Fursat ki gunjaish nahi hai... Sabko saman hai, Khali makan hai, Apne bhi naseeb mein kambakht wahi aasman hai... Mitti ki bas pehchan nahi hai, Hogi bhi to kaise bhala, Wakht jo hamare pass nahi hai... Agey badhna ka jazba to hai, par pichhe dekhne ki himmat kaha, Kaamyaabi ki kashmakash mein, krutagyata ki parchhai nahi hai... Kuchh to badal denge jarur, apni takdeer khud likhenge, Abhi nahin par baadmein kabhi, kyunki... Wakht kisike pass nahin hai! — ssp Everyone has many thoughts but no time. Everyone speaks but no one listens. Art flourishes but audiences disappear. Relationships soften but distances deepen. We all live under the same sky but feel rootless. We'll change things — but later, because time is never with us.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Insan kayin, bas dikkat yahin hai,<br/>\n        Ki wakht kisike pass nahin hai...<br/>\n        Sochte sab, khwaishein nayin hai,<br/>\n        Bin badal kisi ne barsaat sahi hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sab bolte jarur, par sirf sunta to koi nahi hai,<br/>\n        Wakht jo kisike, pass nahin hai...<br/>\n        Ganomein dhun badli jarur,<br/>\n        Par kavita ke alfaz wohi hai...<br/>\n        Rachanatmak kalakar jarur, jaankar aj shrota nahi hai,<br/>\n        Wakht jo kisike, pass nahin hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Rishton mein narmai jarur,<br/>\n        Par faasion ki gehrai rahi hai...<br/>\n        Ehmiyaat ka sheesha saamne rakhe bina,<br/>\n        Fursat ki gunjaish nahi hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Sabko saman hai, Khali makan hai,<br/>\n        Apne bhi naseeb mein kambakht wahi aasman hai...<br/>\n        Mitti ki bas pehchan nahi hai, Hogi bhi to kaise bhala,<br/>\n        Wakht jo hamare pass nahi hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Agey badhna ka jazba to hai, par pichhe dekhne ki himmat kaha,<br/>\n        Kaamyaabi ki kashmakash mein, krutagyata ki parchhai nahi hai...<br/>\n        Kuchh to badal denge jarur, apni takdeer khud likhenge,<br/>\n        Abhi nahin par baadmein kabhi, kyunki...<br/>\n        Wakht kisike pass nahin hai!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Everyone has many thoughts but no time. Everyone speaks but no one listens. Art flourishes but audiences disappear. Relationships soften but distances deepen. We all live under the same sky but feel rootless. We'll change things — but later, because time is never with us.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":75,"id":"poem-75","title":"Har Hrutu Mein Alag Sawera","subtitle":"Every Season, a New Dawn","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Every season brings a different dawn, every rain a different journey. In every direction, every pair of eyes holds a different view of the very same world.","searchText":"Poem 75 Har Hrutu Mein Alag Sawera Every Season, a New Dawn Har hrutu mein alag sawera, Har barish mein alag guzara. Jis disha bhi chalein jahan mein, Har ankhon mein alag nazara! — ssp Every season brings a different dawn, every rain a different journey. In every direction, every pair of eyes holds a different view of the very same world.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Har hrutu mein alag sawera,<br/>\n        Har barish mein alag guzara.<br/>\n        Jis disha bhi chalein jahan mein,<br/>\n        Har ankhon mein alag nazara!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Every season brings a different dawn, every rain a different journey. In every direction, every pair of eyes holds a different view of the very same world.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":76,"id":"poem-76","title":"Dil Ki Laparwahi","subtitle":"The Heart's Carelessness","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"The heart became so careless that it forgot to ask how you were. Your loneliness was such that I forgot to walk beside you. When life tests you like this, we even forget to simply pass through.","searchText":"Poem 76 Dil Ki Laparwahi The Heart's Carelessness Dil ki laparwahi aisi... Ki haal puchhna hi bhul gaye, Unki ek tanhayee aisi, Ki sath chalna hi bhul gaye! Phir kiski majal chalein, Inn halaton ke saamne... Wakht ke imtehan mein dekho, Hum guzrna hi bhul gaye! — ssp The heart became so careless that it forgot to ask how you were. Your loneliness was such that I forgot to walk beside you. When life tests you like this, we even forget to simply pass through.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dil ki laparwahi aisi...<br/>\n        Ki haal puchhna hi bhul gaye,<br/>\n        Unki ek tanhayee aisi,<br/>\n        Ki sath chalna hi bhul gaye!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Phir kiski majal chalein,<br/>\n        Inn halaton ke saamne...<br/>\n        Wakht ke imtehan mein dekho,<br/>\n        Hum guzrna hi bhul gaye!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The heart became so careless that it forgot to ask how you were. Your loneliness was such that I forgot to walk beside you. When life tests you like this, we even forget to simply pass through.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":77,"id":"poem-77","title":"Aasman Mein Udna Ho Toh","subtitle":"If You Wish to Fly","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"If you want to soar, why keep looking down at the earth? If you want to turn in every direction, how will you keep every promise? Don't celebrate the stars when you want the moon. The question is: why does everyone scramble daily for a happy life, yet so rarely find one?","searchText":"Poem 77 Aasman Mein Udna Ho Toh If You Wish to Fly Aasman mein udna ho toh, Kyu dharti se nazar milayein... Har disha mein mudna ho toh, Kaise har ek ka wachan nibhayein... Chand sametne ki ichha jab mann mein, Kyu sitaronka jashn manayein... Khushhal Zindagi ko badi banane, Kyu har koi har roj jutt jayein... — ssp If you want to soar, why keep looking down at the earth? If you want to turn in every direction, how will you keep every promise? Don't celebrate the stars when you want the moon. The question is: why does everyone scramble daily for a happy life, yet so rarely find one?","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Aasman mein udna ho toh,<br/>\n        Kyu dharti se nazar milayein...<br/>\n        Har disha mein mudna ho toh,<br/>\n        Kaise har ek ka wachan nibhayein...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Chand sametne ki ichha jab mann mein,<br/>\n        Kyu sitaronka jashn manayein...<br/>\n        Khushhal Zindagi ko badi banane,<br/>\n        Kyu har koi har roj jutt jayein...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">If you want to soar, why keep looking down at the earth? If you want to turn in every direction, how will you keep every promise? Don't celebrate the stars when you want the moon. The question is: why does everyone scramble daily for a happy life, yet so rarely find one?</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":78,"id":"poem-78","title":"Badalonke Surat Mein","subtitle":"In the Shape of Clouds","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"The moon has a story hidden in cloud shapes — a wandering dreamer's untold tale. He searches for a destination even God doesn't know. Look within for the secret that drives you — it's everyone's story. We must run and also learn to rise after falling.","searchText":"Poem 78 Badalonke Surat Mein In the Shape of Clouds Badalonke surat mein, ye chanda ki kahani hai... Ek deewane musafir ki, ye ankahi jubani hai... Chal pada hai woh uss, manzil ko talashte hue, Jis mukaam ki na usko, na khuda ko koi nishani hai... Konsa raaz hai phir aisa, jo usko takad deta ho, Jara khudse puchhke dekho janab, Ye aapki aur meri nahi, Har ek ki kahani hai! Iss safar mein hume bhaagna hai, hume hi gir ke sawarna hai... Kyunki aur kisi ki ho na ho, Yahan chalti bas apni manmani hai! — ssp The moon has a story hidden in cloud shapes — a wandering dreamer's untold tale. He searches for a destination even God doesn't know. Look within for the secret that drives you — it's everyone's story. We must run and also learn to rise after falling.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Badalonke surat mein, ye chanda ki kahani hai...<br/>\n        Ek deewane musafir ki, ye ankahi jubani hai...<br/>\n        Chal pada hai woh uss, manzil ko talashte hue,<br/>\n        Jis mukaam ki na usko, na khuda ko koi nishani hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Konsa raaz hai phir aisa, jo usko takad deta ho,<br/>\n        Jara khudse puchhke dekho janab,<br/>\n        Ye aapki aur meri nahi,<br/>\n        Har ek ki kahani hai!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Iss safar mein hume bhaagna hai, hume hi gir ke sawarna hai...<br/>\n        Kyunki aur kisi ki ho na ho,<br/>\n        Yahan chalti bas apni manmani hai!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The moon has a story hidden in cloud shapes — a wandering dreamer's untold tale. He searches for a destination even God doesn't know. Look within for the secret that drives you — it's everyone's story. We must run and also learn to rise after falling.</div>\n","featuredRank":17},{"number":79,"id":"poem-79","title":"Mitti Banne Taiyyar","subtitle":"Ready to Become Earth","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Ready to be earth — just promise to be the rain. Ready to hold fragrance within — just promise to become the gentle request. A metaphor for pure, selfless readiness in love.","searchText":"Poem 79 Mitti Banne Taiyyar Ready to Become Earth Mitti banne taiyyar baithe hai, Bas baarish banne ka wada karo... Ittar chhupaye mehmaan baithe hai, Ek guzarish banne ka wada karo.... — ssp Ready to be earth — just promise to be the rain. Ready to hold fragrance within — just promise to become the gentle request. A metaphor for pure, selfless readiness in love.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Mitti banne taiyyar baithe hai,<br/>\n        Bas baarish banne ka wada karo...<br/>\n        Ittar chhupaye mehmaan baithe hai,<br/>\n        Ek guzarish banne ka wada karo....\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Ready to be earth — just promise to be the rain. Ready to hold fragrance within — just promise to become the gentle request. A metaphor for pure, selfless readiness in love.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":80,"id":"poem-80","title":"Dilkhulas Hasya Agdi","subtitle":"Wholehearted Joy — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Full-hearted laughter, fulfilling joy — and immediately, the feeling of touching the sky. Such a simple verse, so deep to truly understand. Stars guide us, and human greatness is built upon this very joy.","searchText":"Poem 80 Dilkhulas Hasya Agdi Wholehearted Joy — (Marathi) Dilkhulas hasya agdi, manmurad lutawe... Lagech te anubhavnaryas, Akash thengne watawe! Itka sopa chhand, ya samajane jopasawa... Nakshatranche dene lagun, Manuski che shikhar gathave! — ssp Full-hearted laughter, fulfilling joy — and immediately, the feeling of touching the sky. Such a simple verse, so deep to truly understand. Stars guide us, and human greatness is built upon this very joy.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Dilkhulas hasya agdi, manmurad lutawe...<br/>\n        Lagech te anubhavnaryas,<br/>\n        Akash thengne watawe!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Itka sopa chhand, ya samajane jopasawa...<br/>\n        Nakshatranche dene lagun,<br/>\n        Manuski che shikhar gathave!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Full-hearted laughter, fulfilling joy — and immediately, the feeling of touching the sky. Such a simple verse, so deep to truly understand. Stars guide us, and human greatness is built upon this very joy.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":81,"id":"poem-81","title":"We Have the Least Control","subtitle":"A Prose Reflection","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"We control nothing before birth or after death. Even within life, control follows a curve — helpless at the start, peaking in midlife, surrendering again toward the end. Life is a gentle arc back to surrender.","searchText":"Poem 81 We Have the Least Control A Prose Reflection We have the least control over our lives and the world around us before our birth and after our death. That part is obvious. What's not so obvious is that even within life, this pattern repeats. When we are born, we have almost no control. As we grow up, our control over our choices and surroundings gradually increases, reaching a kind of peak somewhere in mid-life. Then, as we age, that control slowly fades again. It's like a curve that rises from helplessness, peaks in self-determination, and then gently returns to surrender. — ssp We control nothing before birth or after death. Even within life, control follows a curve — helpless at the start, peaking in midlife, surrendering again toward the end. Life is a gentle arc back to surrender.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        We have the least control over our lives and the world around us before our birth and after our death. That part is obvious.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        What's not so obvious is that even within life, this pattern repeats. When we are born, we have almost no control. As we grow up, our control over our choices and surroundings gradually increases, reaching a kind of peak somewhere in mid-life. Then, as we age, that control slowly fades again.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        It's like a curve that rises from helplessness, peaks in self-determination, and then gently returns to surrender.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">We control nothing before birth or after death. Even within life, control follows a curve — helpless at the start, peaking in midlife, surrendering again toward the end. Life is a gentle arc back to surrender.</div>\n","featuredRank":14},{"number":82,"id":"poem-82","title":"Surya Kade Pahun","subtitle":"Looking at the Sun — (Marathi)","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"A chain of wonder at nature — the sun, the moon, the sea, rivers, and the smallest living things — ending with a quiet question: how do we forget the gifts that all of existence gives us?","searchText":"Poem 82 Surya Kade Pahun Looking at the Sun — (Marathi) Surya kade pahun nawal watte, Chandra peksha itka motha kasa? Chandra kade pahun nawal watte, Samudrat bhar toh ghalto kasa? Samudra kade pahun nawal watte, Rastyatil pratyek nadi bharto kasa? Nadikade pahun nawal watte, Osad srushtit jeev ante kashi? Yatil kahi jeevankade pahun nawal watte, Ya sarvanchi den wisarto kasa? — ssp A chain of wonder at nature — the sun, the moon, the sea, rivers, and the smallest living things — ending with a quiet question: how do we forget the gifts that all of existence gives us?","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body mr\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Surya kade pahun nawal watte,<br/>\n        Chandra peksha itka motha kasa?<br/>\n        Chandra kade pahun nawal watte,<br/>\n        Samudrat bhar toh ghalto kasa?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Samudra kade pahun nawal watte,<br/>\n        Rastyatil pratyek nadi bharto kasa?<br/>\n        Nadikade pahun nawal watte,<br/>\n        Osad srushtit jeev ante kashi?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Yatil kahi jeevankade pahun nawal watte,<br/>\n        Ya sarvanchi den wisarto kasa?\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A chain of wonder at nature — the sun, the moon, the sea, rivers, and the smallest living things — ending with a quiet question: how do we forget the gifts that all of existence gives us?</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":83,"id":"poem-83","title":"Kab Kya Sunte Ho","subtitle":"When You Listen Matters","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"When you listen matters. When you speak matters. Nothing is inherently good or bad — it's always about the right moment. Whether you remember this or not: that is what matters most.","searchText":"Poem 83 Kab Kya Sunte Ho When You Listen Matters Kab kya sunte ho, ye maayne rakhta hai... Kab kya bolte ho, ye maayne rakhta hai... Achha bura to kuch nahi, sab uchit pal ka khel hai sarkar, Ab ye yaad rakhte ho ya nahi, Bas ye maayne rakhta hai! — ssp When you listen matters. When you speak matters. Nothing is inherently good or bad — it's always about the right moment. Whether you remember this or not: that is what matters most.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kab kya sunte ho,<br/>\n        ye maayne rakhta hai...<br/>\n        Kab kya bolte ho,<br/>\n        ye maayne rakhta hai...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Achha bura to kuch nahi,<br/>\n        sab uchit pal ka khel hai sarkar,<br/>\n        Ab ye yaad rakhte ho ya nahi,<br/>\n        Bas ye maayne rakhta hai!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">When you listen matters. When you speak matters. Nothing is inherently good or bad — it's always about the right moment. Whether you remember this or not: that is what matters most.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":84,"id":"poem-84","title":"Nazara Wohi","subtitle":"Same View, Different Worlds","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"The view was the same, but their worlds were entirely different. Both had solutions — just different problems. Every destination had success written into it — only the effort required was different.","searchText":"Poem 84 Nazara Wohi Same View, Different Worlds Nazara wohi par kaaynat alag thhi, Hal donoke pass thha, bas musibatein alag thhi! Har manzil kaamyabi jarur likhi thhi, Bas inki apni apni, koshish hi alag thhi! — ssp The view was the same, but their worlds were entirely different. Both had solutions — just different problems. Every destination had success written into it — only the effort required was different.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Nazara wohi par kaaynat alag thhi,<br/>\n        Hal donoke pass thha, bas musibatein alag thhi!<br/>\n        Har manzil kaamyabi jarur likhi thhi,<br/>\n        Bas inki apni apni, koshish hi alag thhi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">The view was the same, but their worlds were entirely different. Both had solutions — just different problems. Every destination had success written into it — only the effort required was different.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":85,"id":"poem-85","title":"Khud Ek Khayal","subtitle":"How to Speak When You Are a Thought","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"If you yourself are just a thought in someone's mind, how can you be tested? If you're simply getting through life, how do you give advice to others? Among the successful, how do we even begin to speak our truth?","searchText":"Poem 85 Khud Ek Khayal How to Speak When You Are a Thought Khud ek khayal ho jo kisika, Usko koi kaise aazmayein... Khud jo koi kaat raha ho zindagi, Wo kisiko sajah kaise sunayein... Har koshish ki rukawton mein, Jinhone hume jeena sikhaya... Unn kamyab logoki mehfil mein, Hum apna arz kaise farmayein..! — ssp If you yourself are just a thought in someone's mind, how can you be tested? If you're simply getting through life, how do you give advice to others? Among the successful, how do we even begin to speak our truth?","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Khud ek khayal ho jo kisika,<br/>\n        Usko koi kaise aazmayein...<br/>\n        Khud jo koi kaat raha ho zindagi,<br/>\n        Wo kisiko sajah kaise sunayein...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Har koshish ki rukawton mein,<br/>\n        Jinhone hume jeena sikhaya...<br/>\n        Unn kamyab logoki mehfil mein,<br/>\n        Hum apna arz kaise farmayein..!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">If you yourself are just a thought in someone's mind, how can you be tested? If you're simply getting through life, how do you give advice to others? Among the successful, how do we even begin to speak our truth?</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":86,"id":"poem-86","title":"Time","subtitle":"A Prose Reflection","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Everything about how happy or sad we feel is decided by time. An absurd amount of power for something that knows only one direction and cannot even pause.","searchText":"Poem 86 Time A Prose Reflection The amount we are happy or sad about something, is all decided by time! What a fucking insane power for a stupid construction that just knows one way to go, literally doesn't even know how to stop. — ssp Everything about how happy or sad we feel is decided by time. An absurd amount of power for something that knows only one direction and cannot even pause.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        The amount we are happy or sad about something, is all decided by time!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        What a fucking insane power for a stupid construction that just knows one way to go, literally doesn't even know how to stop.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Everything about how happy or sad we feel is decided by time. An absurd amount of power for something that knows only one direction and cannot even pause.</div>\n","featuredRank":6},{"number":87,"id":"poem-87","title":"Kaise?","subtitle":"How?","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"How can you achieve success if you don't first find a path better than the goal itself? How can you truly understand someone after just one meeting? And how can you sleep well when you go to bed carrying today's grief and tomorrow's worry?","searchText":"Poem 87 Kaise? How? Suraj ugte hi kaam par jate, Har manzar se dil behlate, Laksh se behtar rastah na lagein, Safalta haasil hogi kaise? Pehli nazar mein jaanna chahte, Ek mulakat mein sab batlate, Samjh se pehle aagey badh gaye janab, Parakh aakhir hogi kaise? Beetein din ki takleef yaad kar, Mushkil kal ka anuman lagate, Har chinta dhyan rakhkar hum jo Sone chale jate, Nind puri hogi kaise? — ssp How can you achieve success if you don't first find a path better than the goal itself? How can you truly understand someone after just one meeting? And how can you sleep well when you go to bed carrying today's grief and tomorrow's worry?","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Suraj ugte hi kaam par jate,<br/>\n        Har manzar se dil behlate,<br/>\n        Laksh se behtar rastah na lagein,<br/>\n        Safalta haasil hogi kaise?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Pehli nazar mein jaanna chahte,<br/>\n        Ek mulakat mein sab batlate,<br/>\n        Samjh se pehle aagey badh gaye janab,<br/>\n        Parakh aakhir hogi kaise?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Beetein din ki takleef yaad kar,<br/>\n        Mushkil kal ka anuman lagate,<br/>\n        Har chinta dhyan rakhkar<br/>\n        hum jo Sone chale jate,<br/>\n        Nind puri hogi kaise?\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">How can you achieve success if you don't first find a path better than the goal itself? How can you truly understand someone after just one meeting? And how can you sleep well when you go to bed carrying today's grief and tomorrow's worry?</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":88,"id":"poem-88","title":"Samjhne Ki Khwaish Nahin","subtitle":"I Don't Want to Be Understood — I Want Restraint","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"I don't wish to be understood — I want the restraint to explain myself well. Not conspiracy, but the courage to write truth. Not the end of customs, but change within some. Not God in stone — but humanity in hearts.","searchText":"Poem 88 Samjhne Ki Khwaish Nahin I Don't Want to Be Understood — I Want Restraint Samjhne ki khwaish nahin, Bas samjhane ka sanyam chahta hu... Jhoot kehne ki saajish nahin, Bas sach likhne ki jurrat chahta hu... Riwazonka ant nahin, Bas kuch mein badlav chahta hu... Pathhar mein bhagwaan nahin, Bas dil mein insaan chahta hu... — ssp I don't wish to be understood — I want the restraint to explain myself well. Not conspiracy, but the courage to write truth. Not the end of customs, but change within some. Not God in stone — but humanity in hearts.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Samjhne ki khwaish nahin,<br/>\n        Bas samjhane ka sanyam chahta hu...<br/>\n        Jhoot kehne ki saajish nahin,<br/>\n        Bas sach likhne ki jurrat chahta hu...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Riwazonka ant nahin,<br/>\n        Bas kuch mein badlav chahta hu...<br/>\n        Pathhar mein bhagwaan nahin,<br/>\n        Bas dil mein insaan chahta hu...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">I don't wish to be understood — I want the restraint to explain myself well. Not conspiracy, but the courage to write truth. Not the end of customs, but change within some. Not God in stone — but humanity in hearts.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":89,"id":"poem-89","title":"Akhir Chahte Kya Ho?","subtitle":"What Do You Actually Want?","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"What do you actually want? Not the habit of steadiness — just permission to slip. Not worship — just a moment of grace. Not obligation — just the warmth of friendship. Not fame in the neighbourhood — just recognition of oneself.","searchText":"Poem 89 Akhir Chahte Kya Ho? What Do You Actually Want? Akhir chahte kya ho? Samhalneki adat nahin, Bas fisalneki ijajat chahta hu... Kisi tarah ki ibadat nahin, Bas do paal ki inayat chahta hu... Ek duje par ehsaan nahin, Bas dosti ka anumaan chahta hu... Mohlle mein zikar nahin, Bas khud ki pehchan chahta hu... — ssp What do you actually want? Not the habit of steadiness — just permission to slip. Not worship — just a moment of grace. Not obligation — just the warmth of friendship. Not fame in the neighbourhood — just recognition of oneself.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Akhir chahte kya ho?<br/>\n        Samhalneki adat nahin,<br/>\n        Bas fisalneki ijajat chahta hu...<br/>\n        Kisi tarah ki ibadat nahin,<br/>\n        Bas do paal ki inayat chahta hu...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Ek duje par ehsaan nahin,<br/>\n        Bas dosti ka anumaan chahta hu...<br/>\n        Mohlle mein zikar nahin,<br/>\n        Bas khud ki pehchan chahta hu...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">What do you actually want? Not the habit of steadiness — just permission to slip. Not worship — just a moment of grace. Not obligation — just the warmth of friendship. Not fame in the neighbourhood — just recognition of oneself.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":90,"id":"poem-90","title":"Panchhiyon Ki Tarah","subtitle":"Like Birds","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Like birds that quietly change homes, like rivers that must keep flowing — seasons teach them to change, and finally the ocean teaches them to still. Nature's way of moving and, eventually, finding rest.","searchText":"Poem 90 Panchhiyon Ki Tarah Like Birds Panchhiyon ki tarah koi, Yun hi ghar badalta hoga... Nadiyon sa bhavuk koi aur, Behna jarur azmata hoga... Uss bahav mein mausam unhe, Badalna sikhata hoga, Kahin ant mein sagar unhe, Theherna samjhata hoga! — ssp Like birds that quietly change homes, like rivers that must keep flowing — seasons teach them to change, and finally the ocean teaches them to still. Nature's way of moving and, eventually, finding rest.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Panchhiyon ki tarah koi,<br/>\n        Yun hi ghar badalta hoga...<br/>\n        Nadiyon sa bhavuk koi aur,<br/>\n        Behna jarur azmata hoga...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Uss bahav mein mausam unhe,<br/>\n        Badalna sikhata hoga,<br/>\n        Kahin ant mein sagar unhe,<br/>\n        Theherna samjhata hoga!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Like birds that quietly change homes, like rivers that must keep flowing — seasons teach them to change, and finally the ocean teaches them to still. Nature's way of moving and, eventually, finding rest.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":91,"id":"poem-91","title":"Koi Hawa Ke Sath Chalkar","subtitle":"Walk with the Wind","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Walk with the wind and you'll end up arguing with clouds. Stretch out and you'll find yourself clinging to the earth. Leaves will teach you to scatter; time will teach you to pass. Look around once — life itself will teach you to stand.","searchText":"Poem 91 Koi Hawa Ke Sath Chalkar Walk with the Wind Koi hawa ke sath chalkar, Badalon se jhagad lega! Koi angdai sath kehkar, Bas dharti se lipat lega! Patte bikharna sikha denge, Wakht guzarna sikha dega! Ek bar aspass dekh loge agar, Zindagi samhalna sikha degi! — ssp Walk with the wind and you'll end up arguing with clouds. Stretch out and you'll find yourself clinging to the earth. Leaves will teach you to scatter; time will teach you to pass. Look around once — life itself will teach you to stand.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Koi hawa ke sath chalkar,<br/>\n        Badalon se jhagad lega!<br/>\n        Koi angdai sath kehkar,<br/>\n        Bas dharti se lipat lega!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Patte bikharna sikha denge,<br/>\n        Wakht guzarna sikha dega!<br/>\n        Ek bar aspass dekh loge agar,<br/>\n        Zindagi samhalna sikha degi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Walk with the wind and you'll end up arguing with clouds. Stretch out and you'll find yourself clinging to the earth. Leaves will teach you to scatter; time will teach you to pass. Look around once — life itself will teach you to stand.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":92,"id":"poem-92","title":"Kab Aur Kaha","subtitle":"Right Time, Right Place","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"It's all about when and where. The right time, the right place — that determines everything. Rain and sun make a rainbow; the moon moves oceans; earth and sun bloom jungles. Know your time, know yourself — and your story will write itself.","searchText":"Poem 92 Kab Aur Kaha Right Time, Right Place Kab aur kaha, ye khel bas isi ka hai... Sahi wakht aur sahi jagah, ye duniya bas uss hi ki hai. Barsaat agar dhoop se mil jaye, Toh saat rang jarur khilenge. Chand agar dharti se judd jaye, Toh khud mahasagar bhi hilenge. Mitti suraj ka milap jo, Toh jungle pura khil uthta hai. Nadi parvaat jutt jaye, Toh srushti ka sangam dikhta hai. Wakht aur apni pehchan rakho bas, Toh kahinse jarur madat milegi... Dhoop mitti chand taron jaisi phir, Apki bhi dastaan banegi! — ssp It's all about when and where. The right time, the right place — that determines everything. Rain and sun make a rainbow; the moon moves oceans; earth and sun bloom jungles. Know your time, know yourself — and your story will write itself.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kab aur kaha, ye khel bas isi ka hai...<br/>\n        Sahi wakht aur sahi jagah,<br/>\n        ye duniya bas uss hi ki hai.<br/>\n        Barsaat agar dhoop se mil jaye,<br/>\n        Toh saat rang jarur khilenge.<br/>\n        Chand agar dharti se judd jaye,<br/>\n        Toh khud mahasagar bhi hilenge.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Mitti suraj ka milap jo,<br/>\n        Toh jungle pura khil uthta hai.<br/>\n        Nadi parvaat jutt jaye,<br/>\n        Toh srushti ka sangam dikhta hai.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wakht aur apni pehchan rakho bas,<br/>\n        Toh kahinse jarur madat milegi...<br/>\n        Dhoop mitti chand taron jaisi phir,<br/>\n        Apki bhi dastaan banegi!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">It's all about when and where. The right time, the right place — that determines everything. Rain and sun make a rainbow; the moon moves oceans; earth and sun bloom jungles. Know your time, know yourself — and your story will write itself.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":93,"id":"poem-93","title":"Purpose","subtitle":"A Prose Reflection","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},"meaning":"Purpose turns discomfort into meaningful sacrifice. When purpose is clear, even pain feels fulfilling. When it disappears, the same pain becomes regret. The real task: hold on to purpose before discomfort takes over.","searchText":"Poem 93 Purpose A Prose Reflection Is it purpose that turns discomfort into meaningful sacrifice? We often sacrifice for our loved ones, our country, or our career. The process can be uncomfortable, but it still feels fulfilling because it serves a higher purpose. When that purpose becomes unclear or disappears, the same discomfort no longer feels like sacrifice. It feels like regret. So perhaps the real task is to hold on to our purpose before the discomfort takes over. — ssp Purpose turns discomfort into meaningful sacrifice. When purpose is clear, even pain feels fulfilling. When it disappears, the same pain becomes regret. The real task: hold on to purpose before discomfort takes over.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Is it purpose that turns discomfort into meaningful sacrifice?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        We often sacrifice for our loved ones, our country, or our career. The process can be uncomfortable, but it still feels fulfilling because it serves a higher purpose. When that purpose becomes unclear or disappears, the same discomfort no longer feels like sacrifice. It feels like regret.\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        So perhaps the real task is to hold on to our purpose before the discomfort takes over.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Purpose turns discomfort into meaningful sacrifice. When purpose is clear, even pain feels fulfilling. When it disappears, the same pain becomes regret. The real task: hold on to purpose before discomfort takes over.</div>\n","featuredRank":13},{"number":94,"id":"poem-94","title":"Naam Bada Karna","subtitle":"Make a Name","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"You'll need to make a name — looks alone won't carry you far. Stay loyal to your country; soldiers' lives are not cheap. Some work simply has to be done by us — we cannot keep waiting for the government.","searchText":"Poem 94 Naam Bada Karna Make a Name Naam bada karna pdega, Surat se pehchan btayi nhi jaati... Durr unhe karna pdega, Kaamyabi jinse dekhi nhi jaati... Insaniyat ko kareeb rkhna pdega, Janazonse dosti seekhi nhi jaati... Khayal sabka karna pdega, Khushhali desh mein aisehi nhi aati... Wafadar watan se rehna pdega, Jaan jawanoki aisehi nhi jaati... Thoda kaam khud hi ko krna pdega, Sarkar har bar apni nhi aati! नाम बड़ा करना पड़ेगा, सूरत से पहचान बताई नहीं जाती... दूर उन्हे करना पड़ेगा, कामियबी जिनसे देखी नहीं जाती... इंसानियत को करीब रखना पड़ेगा, जनाजोसे दोस्ती किनी नहीं जाती... खयाल सबका करना पड़ेगा, खुशहाली देश में ऐसेही नहीं आती... वफादार वतन से रहना पड़ेगा, जान जवानोकी ऐसीही नहीं जाती... थोड़ा काम हम ही को करना पड़ेगा दोस्त, सरकार हर बार अपनी नहीं आती... — ssp You'll need to make a name — looks alone won't carry you far. Stay loyal to your country; soldiers' lives are not cheap. Some work simply has to be done by us — we cannot keep waiting for the government.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Naam bada karna pdega,<br/>\n          Surat se pehchan btayi nhi jaati...<br/>\n          Durr unhe karna pdega,<br/>\n          Kaamyabi jinse dekhi nhi jaati...\n        </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Insaniyat ko kareeb rkhna pdega,<br/>\n          Janazonse dosti seekhi nhi jaati...<br/>\n          Khayal sabka karna pdega,<br/>\n          Khushhali desh mein aisehi nhi aati...\n        </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Wafadar watan se rehna pdega,<br/>\n          Jaan jawanoki aisehi nhi jaati...<br/>\n          Thoda kaam khud hi ko krna pdega,<br/>\n          Sarkar har bar apni nhi aati!\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          नाम बड़ा करना पड़ेगा,<br/>\n          सूरत से पहचान बताई नहीं जाती...<br/>\n          दूर उन्हे करना पड़ेगा,<br/>\n          कामियबी जिनसे देखी नहीं जाती...\n        </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          इंसानियत को करीब रखना पड़ेगा,<br/>\n          जनाजोसे दोस्ती किनी नहीं जाती...<br/>\n          खयाल सबका करना पड़ेगा,<br/>\n          खुशहाली देश में ऐसेही नहीं आती...\n        </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          वफादार वतन से रहना पड़ेगा,<br/>\n          जान जवानोकी ऐसीही नहीं जाती...<br/>\n          थोड़ा काम हम ही को करना पड़ेगा दोस्त,<br/>\n          सरकार हर बार अपनी नहीं आती...\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">You'll need to make a name — looks alone won't carry you far. Stay loyal to your country; soldiers' lives are not cheap. Some work simply has to be done by us — we cannot keep waiting for the government.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":95,"id":"poem-95","title":"Nam Jaan Kar","subtitle":"What Will Knowing My Name Achieve?","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"What will knowing my name achieve? All gods are acceptable to me. History is open for those brave enough to seek truth. I measure good days by my own effort, not the stars. Those who walk with me — I call my own.","searchText":"Poem 95 Nam Jaan Kar What Will Knowing My Name Achieve? Nam jaan kar kya kroge? Hazil ho kuch to bol deta hu... Mazhab se kitna kya smjhoge? Sare bhagwan to pooj deta hu... Janke kuch achha hua to hai nhi, Yakin na ho to bol deta hu... Sachhai janne ki takad ho to, Itihas ke panne khol deta hu... Chand - suraj se nhi apni mehnat se achhe din jaan leta hu, Khuda jaankar pehchan nhi krta, apna kehkar dost maan leta hu... Koshish karo sath chalneki, har manzil ek inam deta hu... Naam jaankar kya kroge? Hasil ho kuch, to bol deta hu...! — ssp What will knowing my name achieve? All gods are acceptable to me. History is open for those brave enough to seek truth. I measure good days by my own effort, not the stars. Those who walk with me — I call my own.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Nam jaan kar kya kroge?<br/>\n        Hazil ho kuch to bol deta hu...<br/>\n        Mazhab se kitna kya smjhoge?<br/>\n        Sare bhagwan to pooj deta hu...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Janke kuch achha hua to hai nhi,<br/>\n        Yakin na ho to bol deta hu...<br/>\n        Sachhai janne ki takad ho to,<br/>\n        Itihas ke panne khol deta hu...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Chand - suraj se nhi apni mehnat se achhe din jaan leta hu,<br/>\n        Khuda jaankar pehchan nhi krta, apna kehkar dost maan leta hu...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Koshish karo sath chalneki, har manzil ek inam deta hu...<br/>\n        Naam jaankar kya kroge? Hasil ho kuch, to bol deta hu...!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">What will knowing my name achieve? All gods are acceptable to me. History is open for those brave enough to seek truth. I measure good days by my own effort, not the stars. Those who walk with me — I call my own.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":96,"id":"poem-96","title":"Badonka Bachpna","subtitle":"Adults Are Becoming Children","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"Adults are becoming childish and children are losing their innocence. In this relentlessly busy world, peaceful sleep is quietly suffocating somewhere.","searchText":"Poem 96 Badonka Bachpna Adults Are Becoming Children Badonka bachpna badh raha hai, Aur bchhon ki masumiyat ghat rahi hai... Ajkal ki iss behat wyast duniya mein, Chain ki nind kahi dum ghut rahi hai... बडोंका बचपना बढ़ रहा है, और बच्चोंकी मासूमियत घट रही है ... आजकल की इस बेहत व्यस्त दुनिया में शायद, चैन की नींद कही दम घुट रही है ...! — ssp Adults are becoming childish and children are losing their innocence. In this relentlessly busy world, peaceful sleep is quietly suffocating somewhere.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"bilingual\">\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          Badonka bachpna badh raha hai,<br/>\n          Aur bchhon ki masumiyat ghat rahi hai...<br/>\n          Ajkal ki iss behat wyast duniya mein,<br/>\n          Chain ki nind kahi dum ghut rahi hai...\n        </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bilingual-sep\"></div>\n<div class=\"poem-body hi\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n          बडोंका बचपना बढ़ रहा है,<br/>\n          और बच्चोंकी मासूमियत घट रही है ...<br/>\n          आजकल की इस बेहत व्यस्त दुनिया में शायद,<br/>\n          चैन की नींद कही दम घुट रही है ...!\n        </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\" style=\"margin-top:28px;\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Adults are becoming childish and children are losing their innocence. In this relentlessly busy world, peaceful sleep is quietly suffocating somewhere.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":97,"id":"poem-97","title":"Wyaparatil Bhav","subtitle":"Values Lost in Trade","languages":["hindi","marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"Prices in markets rise while values in society fall. Daily spectacles of division and violence — the nation split, though blood runs the same colour everywhere.","searchText":"Poem 97 Wyaparatil Bhav Values Lost in Trade Wyaparatil bhav wadhtoy ani samajatil bhav kmi hotoy... Roj roj ka tandav dekhe, jwala ek khayal hai... Rang saman aur khoon laal phir bhi... Batkar desh halaal hai... — ssp Prices in markets rise while values in society fall. Daily spectacles of division and violence — the nation split, though blood runs the same colour everywhere.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Wyaparatil bhav wadhtoy ani samajatil bhav kmi hotoy...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Roj roj ka tandav dekhe, jwala ek khayal hai...<br/>\n        Rang saman aur khoon laal phir bhi...<br/>\n        Batkar desh halaal hai...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Prices in markets rise while values in society fall. Daily spectacles of division and violence — the nation split, though blood runs the same colour everywhere.</div>\n","featuredRank":18},{"number":98,"id":"poem-98","title":"Kahani Toh Adhuri","subtitle":"At Least Finish the Poem","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"Your story may be incomplete — but at least finish the poem, sir. A wry, affectionate nudge to someone who has given up halfway.","searchText":"Poem 98 Kahani Toh Adhuri At Least Finish the Poem Kahani toh adhuri hi hai aapki, Kamaskam shayari toh puri kar lo janab! — ssp Your story may be incomplete — but at least finish the poem, sir. A wry, affectionate nudge to someone who has given up halfway.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Kahani toh adhuri hi hai aapki,<br/>\n        Kamaskam shayari toh puri kar lo janab!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Your story may be incomplete — but at least finish the poem, sir. A wry, affectionate nudge to someone who has given up halfway.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":99,"id":"poem-99","title":"Meri Apni Kahani","subtitle":"My Own Story","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},"meaning":"In my own story so far, other people's tales take up more space. And in the estate of gratitude, parents still hold the largest share.","searchText":"Poem 99 Meri Apni Kahani My Own Story Meri apni kahani mein abtak, Bakiyonke hi kisse jyada hai... Ehsaano ki jaaydaad mein abhi bhi, Ma baap ke hi hisse jyada hai! — ssp In my own story so far, other people's tales take up more space. And in the estate of gratitude, parents still hold the largest share.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Meri apni kahani mein abtak,<br/>\n        Bakiyonke hi kisse jyada hai...<br/>\n        Ehsaano ki jaaydaad mein abhi bhi,<br/>\n        Ma baap ke hi hisse jyada hai!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">In my own story so far, other people's tales take up more space. And in the estate of gratitude, parents still hold the largest share.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":100,"id":"poem-100","title":"The Language You Speak","subtitle":"An Inquiry into Identity","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},"meaning":"A rapid-fire inquiry into identity — language, genes, emotions, the present moment — all dismissed one by one. The conclusion: you're just an abstraction. A playful yet genuinely deep question about what defines a person.","searchText":"Poem 100 The Language You Speak An Inquiry into Identity The language you speak? I don't understand! The voices you hear? Make it more clear! It's just the gene bruh? But I'm wearing shorts! How true one is? Oh I lie a lot! Well then the interaction? Ah that might be it... Oh the present emotion? That actually sounds lit... Hey, the current moment? It's passing so quickly... You're just an abstraction! That explains it pretty neatly! — ssp A rapid-fire inquiry into identity — language, genes, emotions, the present moment — all dismissed one by one. The conclusion: you're just an abstraction. A playful yet genuinely deep question about what defines a person.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        The language you speak? I don't understand!<br/>\n        The voices you hear? Make it more clear!<br/>\n        It's just the gene bruh? But I'm wearing shorts!<br/>\n        How true one is? Oh I lie a lot!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Well then the interaction? Ah that might be it...<br/>\n        Oh the present emotion? That actually sounds lit...<br/>\n        Hey, the current moment? It's passing so quickly...<br/>\n        You're just an abstraction! That explains it pretty neatly!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A rapid-fire inquiry into identity — language, genes, emotions, the present moment — all dismissed one by one. The conclusion: you're just an abstraction. A playful yet genuinely deep question about what defines a person.</div>\n","featuredRank":15},{"number":101,"id":"poem-101","title":"What Defines You","subtitle":"An Unanswered Question","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},"meaning":"What exactly is 'you'? Not the body (it ages), not the brain (it changes), not mood (it shifts), not heartbeat (it spikes), not the people around or the place you stand. Not even dreams or the past. The self remains stubbornly undefined.","searchText":"Poem 101 What Defines You An Unanswered Question What defines \"you\" exactly? Is it your body? But it ages everyday... Is it your brain? But it develops everyday.... Is it your mood? Oh varies by minutes... Is it the heartbeat? Oh rises in seconds... People around you? How's that possible... Place where you are? Come on, impossible... What about your dreams? Those aren't real though... And your past? Well that's dead no! — ssp What exactly is 'you'? Not the body (it ages), not the brain (it changes), not mood (it shifts), not heartbeat (it spikes), not the people around or the place you stand. Not even dreams or the past. The self remains stubbornly undefined.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        What defines \"you\" exactly?<br/>\n        Is it your body? But it ages everyday...<br/>\n        Is it your brain? But it develops everyday....<br/>\n        Is it your mood? Oh varies by minutes...<br/>\n        Is it the heartbeat? Oh rises in seconds...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        People around you? How's that possible...<br/>\n        Place where you are? Come on, impossible...<br/>\n        What about your dreams? Those aren't real though...<br/>\n        And your past? Well that's dead no!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">What exactly is 'you'? Not the body (it ages), not the brain (it changes), not mood (it shifts), not heartbeat (it spikes), not the people around or the place you stand. Not even dreams or the past. The self remains stubbornly undefined.</div>\n","featuredRank":16},{"number":102,"id":"poem-102","title":"So Easy to Forget","subtitle":"The Paradox of Being Human","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},"meaning":"A list of human contradictions — forgetting is easy, remembering is hard; letting go is easy, holding on is not. We speak easily but listen poorly, make mistakes easily but forgive rarely. Why are we like this? Easy to ask — difficult to answer.","searchText":"Poem 102 So Easy to Forget The Paradox of Being Human So easy to forget, but difficult to remember. So easy to let go, but difficult to hold on. Why are humans like that? It's so easy to ask, But difficult to answer! So easy to speak, but difficult to listen. So easy to interpret, but difficult to understand. So easy to enact, but difficult to behave. So easy to follow, but difficult to lead. So easy to make a mistake, but difficult to forgive. So easy to justify, but difficult to accept. — ssp A list of human contradictions — forgetting is easy, remembering is hard; letting go is easy, holding on is not. We speak easily but listen poorly, make mistakes easily but forgive rarely. Why are we like this? Easy to ask — difficult to answer.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        So easy to forget, but difficult to remember.<br/>\n        So easy to let go, but difficult to hold on.<br/>\n        Why are humans like that?<br/>\n        It's so easy to ask,<br/>\n        But difficult to answer!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        So easy to speak, but difficult to listen.<br/>\n        So easy to interpret, but difficult to understand.<br/>\n        So easy to enact, but difficult to behave.<br/>\n        So easy to follow, but difficult to lead.<br/>\n        So easy to make a mistake, but difficult to forgive.<br/>\n        So easy to justify, but difficult to accept.\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A list of human contradictions — forgetting is easy, remembering is hard; letting go is easy, holding on is not. We speak easily but listen poorly, make mistakes easily but forgive rarely. Why are we like this? Easy to ask — difficult to answer.</div>\n","featuredRank":5},{"number":103,"id":"poem-103","title":"Keep Smiling on the Horizon","subtitle":"An English Verse","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},"meaning":"Keep smiling from wherever you are, swim across and find me. Don't forget to say hello. Stay near in thought. We're here for a long time — let's enjoy the ride.","searchText":"Poem 103 Keep Smiling on the Horizon An English Verse Keep smiling on the horizon, Swim the ocean and meet me... Next time we meet alone, Don't forget to greet me! Stay there in the thoughts, Here by the side... We are here for very long, Let's enjoy the ride! — ssp Keep smiling from wherever you are, swim across and find me. Don't forget to say hello. Stay near in thought. We're here for a long time — let's enjoy the ride.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Keep smiling on the horizon,<br/>\n        Swim the ocean and meet me...<br/>\n        Next time we meet alone,<br/>\n        Don't forget to greet me!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Stay there in the thoughts,<br/>\n        Here by the side...<br/>\n        We are here for very long,<br/>\n        Let's enjoy the ride!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">Keep smiling from wherever you are, swim across and find me. Don't forget to say hello. Stay near in thought. We're here for a long time — let's enjoy the ride.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":104,"id":"poem-104","title":"There Are Just a Few Days","subtitle":"An English Verse","languages":["english"],"theme":{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},"meaning":"A few rare days when your night is mine and we wake to the same dawn. Life continues in other days too, but we miss those precious few — when time is short and hugs are overdue. Come join me in the promise of small, joyful things.","searchText":"Poem 104 There Are Just a Few Days An English Verse There are just a few days, When your night is mine... The day rises for both, At the same time! I know life's in other days too, But we miss those few... When the moments are short, And many hugs are due! Anyway come join me, In the promise of little things... Those that we aspire, And those which bring joy within! — ssp A few rare days when your night is mine and we wake to the same dawn. Life continues in other days too, but we miss those precious few — when time is short and hugs are overdue. Come join me in the promise of small, joyful things.","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        There are just a few days,<br/>\n        When your night is mine...<br/>\n        The day rises for both,<br/>\n        At the same time!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        I know life's in other days too,<br/>\n        But we miss those few...<br/>\n        When the moments are short,<br/>\n        And many hugs are due!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Anyway come join me,<br/>\n        In the promise of little things...<br/>\n        Those that we aspire,<br/>\n        And those which bring joy within!\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A few rare days when your night is mine and we wake to the same dawn. Life continues in other days too, but we miss those precious few — when time is short and hugs are overdue. Come join me in the promise of small, joyful things.</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":105,"id":"poem-105","title":"नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ?","subtitle":"Naye Panne · 2021-02-18","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"naye-panne","label":"Naye Panne","description":"Newer poems"},"meaning":"A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/CLbuj8jl5y9/","searchText":"Poem 105 नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ? Naye Panne · 2021-02-18 नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ? हासिल हो कुछ तो बोल देता हूं ... मजहब से भी क्या समझोगे ? सारे भगवान तो पूज देता हूं ... जानकर कुछ अच्छा हुआ तो है नहीं, यकीन ना हो तो बोल देता हूं ... सच्चाई जानने की ताकद रखते हो, तो इतिहास के पन्ने खोल देता हूं ... चांद सूरज से नहीं, अपनी मेहनत से अच्छे दिन जान लेता हूं ... खुदा जानकर पहचान नहीं करता, अपना कहकर दोस्त मान लेता हूं ... कोशिश करो भाई साथ चलनेकी, हर मंजिल एक इनाम देता हूं ... नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ? हासिल हो कुछ तो बोल देता हूं ... — ssp A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/CLbuj8jl5y9/","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ?<br/>\n        हासिल हो कुछ तो बोल देता हूं ...<br/>\n        मजहब से भी क्या समझोगे ?<br/>\n        सारे भगवान तो पूज देता हूं ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जानकर कुछ अच्छा हुआ तो है नहीं,<br/>\n        यकीन ना हो तो बोल देता हूं ...<br/>\n        सच्चाई जानने की ताकद रखते हो,<br/>\n        तो इतिहास के पन्ने खोल देता हूं ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        चांद सूरज से नहीं, अपनी मेहनत से अच्छे दिन जान लेता हूं ...<br/>\n        खुदा जानकर पहचान नहीं करता, अपना कहकर दोस्त मान लेता हूं ...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कोशिश करो भाई साथ चलनेकी,<br/>\n        हर मंजिल एक इनाम देता हूं ...<br/>\n        नाम जानकर क्या करोगे ?<br/>\n        हासिल हो कुछ तो बोल देता हूं ...\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/CLbuj8jl5y9/</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":106,"id":"poem-106","title":"आखिर जरूरी क्या है?","subtitle":"Naye Panne · 2021-05-04","languages":["hindi"],"theme":{"slug":"naye-panne","label":"Naye Panne","description":"Newer poems"},"meaning":"A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/COdP8Q4H3RJ/","searchText":"Poem 106 आखिर जरूरी क्या है? Naye Panne · 2021-05-04 आखिर जरूरी क्या है? कामयाब होना जरूरी है, या मिलने पर उसे मेहसूस करना... प्यार करना जरूरी है, या उसका खुलकर इजहार करना... कुछ तो मायने रखता होगा, बस शायद मुझे ही इल्म ना हो... एक बार बता दो, अगर पता हो, आखिर जरूरी क्या है? गलती करना जरूरी है, या उसे माफ करना... गुनाह करना जरूरी है, या उसपर इंसाफ करना... कुछ तो होगा जिसलिये सब लगे पड़े है इस उलझन में... शिकायत नहीं, बस संभ्रम है मन में की, आखिर जरूरी क्या है? शीशे में खुदको देखना जरूरी है, या लोगोकी पेहचान रखना... देश परिवार का हाथ थामना जरूरी है, या खुदकी तरक्की का नगमा... कश्मकश तो यही गुमराह करती है, जल्दी बता दो ताकी सम्हाल पाए भाई की, आखिर जरूरी क्या है? मन्नत मांगना जरूरी है, या कोशिश करना... माथा टेकना जरूरी है, या उसे कभी ना झुकने देना... सारी गलत फहमिया इसीसे तो है संसार में, अब संदेह दूर कर ही लेते है की, आखिर जरूरी क्या है? सोचो... क्या सच में जरूरत है किसी चीज की? या सब ऐसेहि बवाल खड़ा है? जिंदगी का मकसद खोजने की कोशिश में, साला हर जीता जागता क्यू बेहाल पड़ा है? दास्तान यही है बस, अंजाम बता दो... सवाल वोही है बस, रास्ता दिखा दो... आखिर... जरूरी क्या है? — ssp A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/COdP8Q4H3RJ/","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आखिर जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कामयाब होना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या मिलने पर उसे मेहसूस करना...<br/>\n        प्यार करना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या उसका खुलकर इजहार करना...<br/>\n        कुछ तो मायने रखता होगा,<br/>\n        बस शायद मुझे ही इल्म ना हो...<br/>\n        एक बार बता दो, अगर पता हो,<br/>\n        आखिर जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        गलती करना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या उसे माफ करना...<br/>\n        गुनाह करना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या उसपर इंसाफ करना...<br/>\n        कुछ तो होगा जिसलिये सब लगे पड़े है इस उलझन में...<br/>\n        शिकायत नहीं, बस संभ्रम है मन में की,<br/>\n        आखिर जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        शीशे में खुदको देखना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या लोगोकी पेहचान रखना...<br/>\n        देश परिवार का हाथ थामना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या खुदकी तरक्की का नगमा...<br/>\n        कश्मकश तो यही गुमराह करती है,<br/>\n        जल्दी बता दो ताकी सम्हाल पाए भाई की,<br/>\n        आखिर जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        मन्नत मांगना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या कोशिश करना...<br/>\n        माथा टेकना जरूरी है,<br/>\n        या उसे कभी ना झुकने देना...<br/>\n        सारी गलत फहमिया इसीसे तो है संसार में,<br/>\n        अब संदेह दूर कर ही लेते है की,<br/>\n        आखिर जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        सोचो...<br/>\n        क्या सच में जरूरत है किसी चीज की?<br/>\n        या सब ऐसेहि बवाल खड़ा है?<br/>\n        जिंदगी का मकसद खोजने की कोशिश में,<br/>\n        साला हर जीता जागता क्यू बेहाल पड़ा है?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        दास्तान यही है बस,<br/>\n        अंजाम बता दो...<br/>\n        सवाल वोही है बस,<br/>\n        रास्ता दिखा दो...\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आखिर... जरूरी क्या है?\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/COdP8Q4H3RJ/</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":107,"id":"poem-107","title":"अमेरिका अशी कशी?","subtitle":"Naye Panne · 2025-09-14","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"naye-panne","label":"Naye Panne","description":"Newer poems"},"meaning":"A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DOmel0gjhvu/","searchText":"Poem 107 अमेरिका अशी कशी? Naye Panne · 2025-09-14 अमेरिका अशी कशी? एक एकटे जगावे, कामाला पुरून उरावे, तरी देखील उसंत नाही, एकही देव पसंत नाही… सगळी यंत्र मात्र हाताशी, ही अमेरिका अशी कशी?! रोज वेस्टर्न हालचाली, उंच इमारती साद घाली, दिवस-उजेड साठवत, बर्फ पाऊस अकाली… माणसे कमी पण जमीन पुरेशी, भाई ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?! जितकी माणस तितक्या तर्हा, मनुष्या पेक्षा म्हणतात कुत्रा बरा… फॉल इथे साडी नाही, झाडांना लागतो, दिसेल तो प्राणी, हा अमरीकी मारून चाखतो… कप माहिती यांना पण ठाऊक नाही बशी, तेजायला ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?! कामावर रुजू व्हायला, सगळे येतात जगभरून काही कामातून जातात, बाकी कमवतात भरभरून… फावल्या वेळात फिरायला , नेत्रदीपक सृष्टी आहे, समाजाला शिस्त इथे, अन् थोरल्यांना दृष्टी आहे… इथल्या स्वप्नांना काही, सीमा च नाही कशी? भाई खरच प्रश्न आहे ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?! इथे येऊन जग कळते, स्वतःचा मात्र विसर पडतो, स्वावलंबी वाटचालीत, आगळा माणूस वेगळाच घडतो… इथे रहिवासी कामचोर आणि पाहुणे मात्र हौशी, निघतो आता, कळवा पत्राने… अमेरिका ही अशी कशी? — ssp A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DOmel0gjhvu/","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        अमेरिका अशी कशी?\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        एक एकटे जगावे, कामाला पुरून उरावे,<br/>\n        तरी देखील उसंत नाही, एकही देव पसंत नाही…<br/>\n        सगळी यंत्र मात्र हाताशी,<br/>\n        ही अमेरिका अशी कशी?!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        रोज वेस्टर्न हालचाली, उंच इमारती साद घाली,<br/>\n        दिवस-उजेड साठवत,  बर्फ पाऊस अकाली…<br/>\n        माणसे कमी पण जमीन पुरेशी,<br/>\n        भाई ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        जितकी माणस तितक्या तर्हा,<br/>\n        मनुष्या पेक्षा म्हणतात कुत्रा बरा…<br/>\n        फॉल इथे साडी नाही, झाडांना लागतो,<br/>\n        दिसेल तो प्राणी, हा अमरीकी मारून चाखतो…<br/>\n        कप माहिती यांना पण ठाऊक नाही बशी,<br/>\n        तेजायला ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कामावर रुजू व्हायला, सगळे येतात जगभरून<br/>\n        काही कामातून जातात, बाकी कमवतात भरभरून…<br/>\n        फावल्या वेळात फिरायला , नेत्रदीपक सृष्टी आहे,<br/>\n        समाजाला शिस्त इथे, अन् थोरल्यांना दृष्टी आहे…<br/>\n        इथल्या स्वप्नांना काही, सीमा च नाही कशी?<br/>\n        भाई खरच प्रश्न आहे ही, अमेरिका अशी कशी?!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        इथे येऊन जग कळते, स्वतःचा मात्र विसर पडतो,<br/>\n        स्वावलंबी वाटचालीत, आगळा माणूस वेगळाच घडतो…<br/>\n        इथे रहिवासी कामचोर आणि पाहुणे मात्र हौशी,<br/>\n        निघतो आता, कळवा पत्राने…<br/>\n        अमेरिका ही अशी कशी?\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DOmel0gjhvu/</div>\n","featuredRank":null},{"number":108,"id":"poem-108","title":"today’s generation","subtitle":"Naye Panne · 2026-02-07","languages":["marathi"],"theme":{"slug":"naye-panne","label":"Naye Panne","description":"Newer poems"},"meaning":"A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DUc9Z0UjpWe/","searchText":"Poem 108 today’s generation Naye Panne · 2026-02-07 Full poem: today’s generation आजची ही होतकरू पिढी, आणि त्यांच्या अनेक रीतभाती… चला ओळख तरी करून देतो, बाकी काम कुठ फार आमच्या हाती… आता नुसते मेल पाठवतो, लिखाण तर आम्ही कधीच सोडलं… मामाच जे पत्र हरवल, तेही आम्हाला स्पॅम मधे सापडलं! अहो डोकं AI चालवेल, आम्ही नुसती बोटं चालवतो… सिरी आलाराम बडवते, आणि अलेक्सा आमची दिवा मालवते! बाहेरच खाऊन आमच्या, पोटात मात्र कायम कळा… बातम्यांचा हा कागद, आज न चाळलेलाच बरा… आम्ही धाकल्यांकडून ट्रेंड शिकतो, आणि थोरल्यांना अक्कल शिकवतो… वाचनाचा धर्म सोडून, लोकांना पोड cast ऐकवतो… कपडे अगदी टाप टीप आमचे, मुखाला नियमित मलम फासतो… शारीरिक असो वा रोग मानसिक, एखादा डॉक्टर हमखास तपासतो! बाकी खाऊन पिऊन सुखी, अगदी नावला पैसे साठवतो… भक्तीची फार हौस नाही, फक्त सणावारला देव आठवतो! आमच्या छोट्या मोठ्या तक्रारी घेऊन मग, आम्हीच आमची समजूत काढतो… घरापासून लांब जाऊनच, ह्या नात्यांमधला गंध वाढतो… पाहता पाहता मग एक दिवस, कालची पिढी आजची होते… मागची आठवण काढता काढता, नशीब पुढचे आयुष्य वाढते… — ssp A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DUc9Z0UjpWe/","contentHtml":"\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"poem-body\">\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        Full poem: today’s generation\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आजची ही होतकरू पिढी,<br/>\n        आणि त्यांच्या अनेक रीतभाती…<br/>\n        चला ओळख तरी करून देतो,<br/>\n        बाकी काम कुठ फार आमच्या हाती…\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आता नुसते मेल पाठवतो,<br/>\n        लिखाण तर आम्ही कधीच सोडलं…<br/>\n        मामाच जे पत्र हरवल,<br/>\n        तेही आम्हाला स्पॅम मधे सापडलं!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        अहो डोकं AI चालवेल,<br/>\n        आम्ही नुसती बोटं चालवतो…<br/>\n        सिरी आलाराम बडवते,<br/>\n        आणि अलेक्सा आमची दिवा मालवते!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        बाहेरच खाऊन आमच्या, पोटात मात्र कायम कळा…<br/>\n        बातम्यांचा हा कागद,  आज न चाळलेलाच बरा…\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आम्ही धाकल्यांकडून ट्रेंड शिकतो,<br/>\n        आणि थोरल्यांना अक्कल शिकवतो…<br/>\n        वाचनाचा धर्म सोडून, लोकांना पोड cast ऐकवतो…\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        कपडे अगदी टाप टीप आमचे,<br/>\n        मुखाला नियमित मलम फासतो…<br/>\n        शारीरिक असो वा रोग मानसिक,<br/>\n        एखादा डॉक्टर हमखास तपासतो!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        बाकी खाऊन पिऊन सुखी,<br/>\n        अगदी नावला पैसे साठवतो…<br/>\n        भक्तीची फार हौस नाही,<br/>\n        फक्त सणावारला देव आठवतो!\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        आमच्या छोट्या मोठ्या तक्रारी घेऊन मग,<br/>\n        आम्हीच आमची समजूत काढतो…<br/>\n        घरापासून लांब जाऊनच,<br/>\n        ह्या नात्यांमधला गंध वाढतो…\n      </div>\n<div class=\"stanza\">\n        पाहता पाहता मग एक दिवस,<br/>\n        कालची पिढी आजची होते…<br/>\n        मागची आठवण काढता काढता,<br/>\n        नशीब पुढचे आयुष्य वाढते…\n      </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem-sig\">— ssp</div>\n<div class=\"poem-meaning\">A later page from the same notebook. Source archive: https://www.instagram.com/p/DUc9Z0UjpWe/</div>\n","featuredRank":null}],"aphorisms":["my words will be printed on hearts not stones...","Key to a long conversation is the right person.","You were talking to your world, I was talking to mine!","Her smile was the same, maybe my eyes started pursuing it differently... Her presence was the same, maybe my heart started beating differently...","99% of who you are is invisible or untouchable — dark matter/energy resembles.","A poem is a fantasy of a paragraph!","Some just collect stones... not all perfect crystals. Some amorphous, some imperfect shapes. But they love to collect. They value their collection... Others, they collect people.","Night is vulnerable... No matter how bright a day passes by, it's always vulnerable.","Give me an empty canvas and I will be able to paint a picture myself! But it's not easy to find a completely empty canvas these days... coz everyone comes with a baggage.","U cant break a man who's already broken... and can't steal a heart which is already taken!","Let your laughter be cheap... not your tears...","Keep your houses clean, then you won't worry about the guests...!","Don't lose the child in you... even if one isn't pregnant!","You can't be in someone's shoes... but you can help them try new ones!","Someone's experiences can be shared... but can't be experienced!","Ur life doesn't need to be miserable for you to be a philosopher!","Most important ingredient of a delicious dish is the hunger.","Best thing about being in a good mood is not knowing exactly why you are in that mood...","Our own experience is the only unique thing we all have in common!","We often tell many things which don't matter much only to those who matter the most.","Work after relaxation is as necessary as relaxation after work.","To be a scientist is to be naive. Truth doesn't care about us. We should care about it.","Since childhood, we were always keen on going out. Now that it's adulthood, we are always looking forward to coming back home.","Applause is optional.... Response is necessary!","If words would have been sufficient to describe everything... what's the use of those eyes!","Talk until the silence isn't awkward anymore!","Find the purpose — the means will follow.","We are on same page, but with different expressions.","Lost opportunities are gained lessons!","Go with the flow and one ends up in the sink!","When you know that journey is life... make someone a part of it... life will be beautiful.","Nothing will be left except satisfaction.","Die with fame than live with shame."],"themes":[{"slug":"ishq","label":"Ishq","description":"Love & longing"},{"slug":"dosti","label":"Dosti","description":"Friendship"},{"slug":"rishtey","label":"Rishtey","description":"Family & bonds"},{"slug":"zindagi","label":"Zindagi","description":"Life & philosophy"},{"slug":"samaj","label":"Samaj","description":"Society"},{"slug":"english-verses","label":"English Verses","description":"Identity & reflection"},{"slug":"naye-panne","label":"Naye Panne","description":"Newer poems"}]};
